"X-Language-Name: Vietnamese\n"

msgid "A Secret the Manifest Is Keeping"
msgstr ""

msgid "Some badges stay secret until you earn them. Keep driving."
msgstr ""

msgid "road"
msgstr ""

msgid "Out on the Road"
msgstr ""

msgid "Clean runs, hard climbs, and the everyday work of hauling freight."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Working Day"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Rest breaks, inspections, traffic, and the rules that keep a driver legal."
msgstr ""

msgid "career"
msgstr ""

msgid "Career and Rank"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Levels, money, and trucks -- the long climb from hire to owner-operator."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Dial and Song Towns"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Stations you catch on the dial, and the towns those songs put on the map."
msgstr ""

msgid "Weather and the Calendar"
msgstr ""

msgid "Rain, snow, fog, and the seasons while you kept driving."
msgstr ""

msgid "places"
msgstr ""

msgid "Places on the Map"
msgstr ""

msgid "Cities, states, and regions you hauled into."
msgstr ""

msgid "hidden"
msgstr ""

msgid "Deep Cuts"
msgstr ""

msgid "A few badges even dispatch doesn't see coming."
msgstr ""

msgid "Breaker, Breaker"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your first load off the board. Just a handle, a load number, and somewhere "
"to be, good buddy."
msgstr ""

msgid "C.W. McCall - Convoy"
msgstr ""

msgid "Loaded and Rolling"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Cargo's aboard and sealed. Eighteen wheels don't roll themselves to the "
"dock."
msgstr ""

msgid "Alabama - Roll On (Eighteen Wheeler)"
msgstr ""

msgid "First Day"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"First load, first dock, and the air built to cut-out. Day one is in the "
"books."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Franklin County Trucking Company - I'm a Trucker"
msgstr ""

msgid "Signed, Sealed, Hauled"
msgstr ""

msgid "Your first load, signed for and gone. Clean paperwork, no fanfare."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dave Dudley - Truck Drivin' Son-of-a-Gun"
msgstr ""

msgid "Beat the Clock, Fewer Days"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You beat the deadline to the dock. Dispatch only reads the timestamp anyway."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dave Dudley - Six Days on the Road"
msgstr ""

msgid "Pretty as a Billboard"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Delivered without a new dent. The rig's still pretty enough for a billboard."
msgstr ""

msgid "Del Reeves - Girl on the Billboard"
msgstr ""

msgid "Slow Rod Lincoln"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A whole run without one speeding strike. You thought hard about the "
"insurance."
msgstr ""

msgid "Commander Cody and His Lost Planet Airmen - Hot Rod Lincoln"
msgstr ""

msgid "Just Can't Wait to Roll"
msgstr ""

msgid "Five deliveries. That itch to roll finally has a stat line."
msgstr ""

msgid "Willie Nelson - On the Road Again"
msgstr ""

msgid "What a Long, Strange Haul"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Ten deliveries. A long, strange road, and the receipts pile up faster than "
"the stories."
msgstr ""

msgid "Grateful Dead - Truckin'"
msgstr ""

msgid "Another Page, Another Town"
msgstr ""

msgid "Career level 3. Another new town, but this chapter pays better."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bob Seger - Turn the Page"
msgstr ""

msgid "Built It a Piece at a Time"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"25,000 dollars banked, a load at a time. Slower than a Cadillac in a "
"lunchbox, but legal."
msgstr ""

msgid "Johnny Cash - One Piece at a Time"
msgstr ""

msgid "Caught the White-Line Bug"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A thousand miles. The white-line fever's in your blood, and the bugs are on "
"the glass."
msgstr ""

msgid "Merle Haggard - White Line Fever"
msgstr ""

msgid "Where the Ribbon Don't End"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One loaded haul over 900 miles. Long enough for the seat cushion to earn "
"seniority."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tiny Harris - Endless Black Ribbon"
msgstr ""

msgid "Kept It Between the Lines"
msgstr ""

msgid "Your first state line with freight aboard, kept between the lines."
msgstr ""

msgid "Johnny Cash - I Walk the Line"
msgstr ""

msgid "Been Most Everywhere, Man"
msgstr ""

msgid "Three states on one route. The map had to clear its throat."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hank Snow - I've Been Everywhere"
msgstr ""

msgid "Three Regions and Ramblin'"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You've worked three freight regions. Dispatch still mispronounces the next "
"one."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bandit Pays the Toll"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One beep at the toll, and the carrier ate it. Accounting took the wheel."
msgstr ""

msgid "Jerry Reed - East Bound and Down"
msgstr ""

msgid "Turns Out, an Easy Run"
msgstr ""

msgid "Over 300 loaded miles without a toll. This run never got the memo."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dave Dudley - There Ain't No Easy Run"
msgstr ""

msgid "World Through a Wet Windshield"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Through the rain, wipers keeping time and your following distance keeping "
"order."
msgstr ""

msgid "Del Reeves - Looking at the World Through a Windshield"
msgstr ""

msgid "A Mile Past the Last Marker"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Snow or crosswind, the trailer stayed in line and out of the headlines."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dick Curless - A Tombstone Every Mile"
msgstr ""

msgid "Foggy Mountain Haul"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fog thick enough to bend a banjo string, and you never lost the road."
msgstr ""

msgid "Flatt & Scruggs - Foggy Mountain Breakdown"
msgstr ""

msgid "Highway to Maybe Not"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You slowed in time for a road hazard. Your brake pedal had other plans."
msgstr ""

msgid "AC/DC - Highway to Hell"
msgstr ""

msgid "Honky-Tonk of Cones"
msgstr ""

msgid "You crept through the cones like each one had a lawyer."
msgstr ""

msgid "John Anderson - Honky Tonk Crowd"
msgstr ""

msgid "Bumper-to-Bumper Blues"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Heavy traffic, and you kept a sane following distance. You let the jam "
"breathe."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tom Cochrane - Life Is a Highway"
msgstr ""

msgid "inspection"
msgstr ""

msgid "Smokey at the Scale"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An inspection with your paperwork in order and your axle weights behaving."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rod Hart - C.B. Savage"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sweetheart of the Truck Stop"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your first rest stop. The romance lasted as long as the vending machine's "
"stare."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Willis Brothers - Truck Stop Cutie"
msgstr ""

msgid "Filler-Up and Keep Truckin'"
msgstr ""

msgid "You topped off before it got dramatic, then kept on truckin'."
msgstr ""

msgid "C.W. McCall - Old Home Filler-Up an' Keep On-a-Truckin' Cafe"
msgstr ""

msgid "Coffee Break, Driver"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your 30-minute break, taken. One more cup, and your knees said thanks."
msgstr ""

msgid "Buck Owens - Truck Drivin' Man"
msgstr ""

msgid "Five-by-Two and Out"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Ten hours in the bunk, and you woke up legal. Unglamorous, and heroic."
msgstr ""

msgid "Red Simpson - Sleeper, Five-By-Two"
msgstr ""

msgid "Mama Warned You About This"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You bunked down before fatigue took the wheel. This time you listened."
msgstr ""

msgid "Merle Haggard - Mama Tried"
msgstr ""

msgid "A Working Man's Receipt"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fixed right at a real garage. An honest bill, and the truck earns its keep "
"again."
msgstr ""

msgid "Merle Haggard - Workin' Man Blues"
msgstr ""

msgid "Soup It Up a Little"
msgstr ""

msgid "Your first upgrade, a small taste of souped-up confidence."
msgstr ""

msgid "Eighteen Wheels and Then Some"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You bought the heavy hauler. The hills got nervous, and so did the fuel "
"bill."
msgstr ""

msgid "Star of the Interstate"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You built air like a pro. Even the fastest rig on the interstate needs its "
"PSI."
msgstr ""

msgid "Deep Purple - Highway Star"
msgstr ""

msgid "Stick-Shift Solo"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You ran in manual. Every clean shift sounds cool until the grade changes "
"key."
msgstr ""

msgid "Pete Drake - Gear Shiftin'"
msgstr ""

msgid "Eastbound and Gone"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load hauled east and on the dock. Eastbound, hammer down, and nobody "
"waited."
msgstr ""

msgid "Westbound, Foot Down"
msgstr ""

msgid "A load hauled west, chasing the sun down to the dock."
msgstr ""

msgid "Little Feat - Willin'"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Mother Road"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A haul between two old Mother Road towns. The neon's faded, but you still "
"got your kicks."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bobby Troup - (Get Your Kicks on) Route 66"
msgstr ""

msgid "Amarillo by Daybreak"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Into Amarillo, load on the dock by daybreak. No pony, but a fine Panhandle "
"dawn."
msgstr ""

msgid "George Strait - Amarillo by Morning"
msgstr ""

msgid "Clear to Phoenix"
msgstr ""

msgid "Freight delivered in Phoenix. The desert never did cool off."
msgstr ""

msgid "Glen Campbell - By the Time I Get to Phoenix"
msgstr ""

msgid "Wichita on the Line"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load signed for in Wichita. A lineman waved; you were watching the wind."
msgstr ""

msgid "Glen Campbell - Wichita Lineman"
msgstr ""

msgid "Lubbock in the Rearview"
msgstr ""

msgid "Out of Lubbock with a load, the hometown shrinking in the mirror."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mac Davis - Texas in My Rear View Mirror"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Bakersfield Sound"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Freight on the dock in Bakersfield. Your air brakes kept the twang's beat."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dwight Yoakam & Buck Owens - Streets of Bakersfield"
msgstr ""

msgid "Tulsa, Right on Schedule"
msgstr ""

msgid "Into Tulsa right on time. The dock was glad to see you."
msgstr ""

msgid "Don Williams - Tulsa Time"
msgstr ""

msgid "Long Live Las Vegas"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load into Las Vegas. You only gambled on the merge, and the house lost."
msgstr ""

msgid "Elvis Presley - Viva Las Vegas"
msgstr ""

msgid "Midnight Freight to Georgia"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Midnight freight into Georgia. No first-class ticket, just a sleeper and a "
"thermos."
msgstr ""

msgid "Gladys Knight & the Pips - Midnight Train to Georgia"
msgstr ""

msgid "Last Load Out of Detroit"
msgstr ""

msgid "A load out of Detroit. Home keeps calling, but freight pays better."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bobby Bare - Detroit City"
msgstr ""

msgid "Been Everywhere, For Real"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You've hauled in every region on the map. That list of towns is finally "
"long enough."
msgstr ""

msgid "Coast-to-Coast Hauler"
msgstr ""

msgid "One run across most of a continent, salt air to salt air."
msgstr ""

msgid "Woody Guthrie - This Land Is Your Land"
msgstr ""

msgid "Fifty Loads Down the Road"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fifty deliveries. The board knows your handle, and the windshield knows "
"every bug."
msgstr ""

msgid "Just Keep Rollin' On"
msgstr ""

msgid "A hundred deliveries, load after load, until the number got serious."
msgstr ""

msgid "Lynyrd Skynyrd - Call Me the Breeze"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ten Thousand Down the Line"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ten thousand miles. The white-line fever is just the job now."
msgstr ""

msgid "Highway Lifer"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fifty thousand miles. The long ribbon of road won't let you walk away."
msgstr ""

msgid "Roger Miller - King of the Road"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hundred-Grand Hood Ornament"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A hundred thousand dollars banked. Slow as a Cadillac a piece at a time, "
"but legal."
msgstr ""

msgid "Veteran of the Long Haul"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Career level 20. Same docks, same diner pie, but the pages turn easier now."
msgstr ""

msgid "CB Royalty"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your reputation pinned the meter. The channel knows your handle, and "
"dispatch takes your word."
msgstr ""

msgid "Five Clean, In a Row"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Five straight on time, undamaged, and ticket-free. Quiet on the CB, good on "
"the paycheck."
msgstr ""

msgid "Red Simpson - I'm a Truck"
msgstr ""

msgid "Long, Hard, and Spotless"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Over 1,200 miles, on time and spotless. No run comes easy, except yours."
msgstr ""

msgid "Paid Like a Boss Hog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One load over 4,000 dollars gross. Big money, on the right side of the law."
msgstr ""

msgid "Waylon Jennings - Good Ol' Boys"
msgstr ""

msgid "Over the Rockies, Spotless"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A mountain grade, and the freight came down clean. The brakes politely "
"declined to fail."
msgstr ""

msgid "Joe Walsh - Rocky Mountain Way"
msgstr ""

msgid "Four Legs and Rolling"
msgstr ""

msgid "One dispatch, four corridors, run nose to tail."
msgstr ""

msgid "Runnin' the County Line"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Freight on a Virginia dock, across a county line worth singing about."
msgstr ""

msgid "49 Winchester - Russell County Line"
msgstr ""

msgid "Birmingham Before the Coffee Kicks In"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Birmingham before the coffee kicked in. You'd been rolling since before the "
"birds."
msgstr ""

msgid "Andrea and Mud - Birmingham, AL 8:30AM"
msgstr ""

msgid "Bluegrass on the Bill of Lading"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load signed for in Kentucky. The grass is blue; the money was green."
msgstr ""

msgid "Brit Taylor - Kentucky Blue"
msgstr ""

msgid "Giant of the Turnpike"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You delivered in New Jersey and lived to merge again. Jughandles and all."
msgstr ""

msgid "Elle King - Jersey Giant"
msgstr ""

msgid "Made It to Waco Just Fine"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Freight into Waco without a scratch. Whatever the songs say, you kept your "
"health."
msgstr ""

msgid "Croy and the Boys - Don't Let Me Die in Waco"
msgstr ""

msgid "Coast Freight by Two O'Clock"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On the Mississippi Gulf Coast by two o'clock. Shrimp boats, salt air, "
"signed bills."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ellis Bullard - Biloxi By Two"
msgstr ""

msgid "An Overnight Success, Eventually"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load in Nashville, where songwriters wait years. Your freight broke "
"through on the first try."
msgstr ""

msgid "Curtis Grimes - Ten Year Town"
msgstr ""

msgid "Freight Up the Holler"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Into Appalachian coal and ridge country, on roads that bend like fiddle "
"tunes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dirty Grass Soul - Back to the Holler"
msgstr ""

msgid "Where the Herds Still Graze"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A delivery in Wyoming. No traffic, just wind, antelope, and the odd legend."
msgstr ""

msgid "Chancey Williams - Land of the Buffalo"
msgstr ""

msgid "Shadow of the Giants"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Up in far Northern California, where the redwoods make a trailer feel small."
msgstr ""

msgid "Andrew Gabbard - Redwood"
msgstr ""

msgid "Pines to the Pacific"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Freight in the Pacific Northwest, where the evergreens crowd the shoulder "
"and the rain sets its own schedule."
msgstr ""

msgid "Colby Acuff - Western White Pines"
msgstr ""

msgid "A Ballad Out West"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Freight into El Paso. The old ballads end in heartbreak; yours ended with a "
"signature."
msgstr ""

msgid "Marty Robbins - El Paso City"
msgstr ""

msgid "Down the Old Cowboy Road"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Freight in Laredo, right on the border. Strictly business, and everybody "
"stayed cheerful."
msgstr ""

msgid "Marty Robbins - Streets of Laredo"
msgstr ""

msgid "Better Off Than Busted Flat"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Into Baton Rouge with a paycheck coming. Beats busted flat with a harmonica."
msgstr ""

msgid "Kris Kristofferson - Me and Bobby McGee"
msgstr ""

msgid "A Whistle Outside Folsom"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Freight into Sacramento. You heard a train whistle near Folsom and kept "
"rolling, free."
msgstr ""

msgid "Johnny Cash - Folsom Prison Blues"
msgstr ""

msgid "All Your Loads Live in Texas"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Both ends of the load inside the Texas Triangle. This week the whole map "
"was one state."
msgstr ""

msgid "George Strait - All My Ex's Live in Texas"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Compass Said Keep Going"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A delivery that ran hard north. You found a bearing, and it had a dock at "
"the end."
msgstr ""

msgid "Caroline Spence - True North"
msgstr ""

msgid "Down the Map with a Load"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A delivery that ran hard south, toward warmer air and somebody waiting on "
"freight."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Allman Brothers Band - Southbound"
msgstr ""

msgid "Right Back Where You Started"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You hauled the next load right back where you started. This week the "
"horizon ran a shuttle."
msgstr ""

msgid "Aaron McDonnell - You Drive Back"
msgstr ""

msgid "Flats, Foothills, and the Big Climb"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Flats, hills, and a real mountain grade on one route. The freight never "
"noticed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ellis Bullard - Roller Coaster"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Long Way to the Dock"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One dispatch longer than a day on the trip clock. The last hundred miles "
"felt personal."
msgstr ""

msgid "Billy Strings - Long Journey Home"
msgstr ""

msgid "Cold Freight, Warm Heart"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your first reefer load, temperature steady. The trailer ran cold; your mood "
"didn't."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hank Williams - Cold, Cold Heart"
msgstr ""

msgid "Big John on the Drive Axles"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your first heavy-haul load. Every gear change felt like moving a legend."
msgstr ""

msgid "Jimmy Dean - Big Bad John"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sparkle in the Dry Van"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your first high-value load, seals intact. It rode quiet and never stopped "
"for souvenirs."
msgstr ""

msgid "Amanda Fields - Diamonds"
msgstr ""

msgid "Chained and Checked"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your first flatbed load, every chain still tight. You checked within the "
"first 50 miles, by the book."
msgstr ""

msgid "Red Simpson - Roll, Truck, Roll"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Load That Pushes Back"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your first tanker load, delivered. The surge tried to drive the whole way. "
"You didn't let it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Two Boxes, One Driver"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your first set of doubles, delivered whole. The rear trailer wandered; the "
"mirrors told the truth."
msgstr ""

msgid "Red Sovine - Giddy-Up Go"
msgstr ""

msgid "Placards Up"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your first placarded load, no incidents. The paperwork rode shotgun. "
"Careful pays."
msgstr ""

msgid "Merle Haggard - Movin' On"
msgstr ""

msgid "Through the Gate"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your first container off the port. Your card got you through the gate."
msgstr ""

msgid "Johnny Cash - I've Been Everywhere"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Long Combination"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your first turnpike doubles run. Two long trailers, and every lane change "
"planned half a mile out."
msgstr ""

msgid "Feed, Seed, and Freight"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Farm freight where it was needed. Somewhere a rancher checked the sky and "
"said much obliged."
msgstr ""

msgid "Emily Nenni - On The Ranch"
msgstr ""

msgid "Grossed Out at the Scale House"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load near the legal weight limit, and the scale house waved it through."
msgstr ""

msgid "Joe Stampley - Roll On Big Mama"
msgstr ""

msgid "Twenty-Five and Rolling Steady"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Twenty-five deliveries, somewhere between rookie and veteran, with more "
"road than most."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ellie Turner - A Little Farther Down The Line"
msgstr ""

msgid "Two Hundred and Playing for Keeps"
msgstr ""

msgid "Two hundred deliveries. That's a body of work."
msgstr ""

msgid "Emily Nenni - Long Game"
msgstr ""

msgid "A Vault with Mud Flaps"
msgstr ""

msgid "250,000 dollars banked. The teller quit counting out loud."
msgstr ""

msgid "Alex Miller - Breaking the Bank"
msgstr ""

msgid "Half a Million in Lifetime Freight"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Half a million dollars earned over your career. Not easy money, but it "
"spends."
msgstr ""

msgid "Brit Taylor - Rich Little Girls"
msgstr ""

msgid "Leave Me on the Interstate"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A hundred thousand miles. The road owns most of you now, but not all of you "
"today."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bob Wayne - Spread My Ashes on the Highway"
msgstr ""

msgid "Strut Past the Fuel Island"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Reputation 90 or better. Stroll the truck stop like you own the coffee "
"machine."
msgstr ""

msgid "Elvin Bishop - Struttin' My Stuff"
msgstr ""

msgid "Thirty Days of Diesel"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A full month on the career clock. Docks, diners, and dawn starts, and you "
"want more."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ellie Turner - One More Day"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Porch Light Was Still On"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With 10 deliveries behind you, you brought a load home. The streets shrank; "
"the welcome didn't."
msgstr ""

msgid "Arlo McKinley - Back Home"
msgstr ""

msgid "Room Enough to Turn Around"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A bobtail move, no trailer. Turning around takes a lot less room without "
"the box."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Willis Brothers - Give Me 40 Acres"
msgstr ""

msgid "Nobody's Fool on the First"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A delivery on April 1. The load was real, and the joke was on nobody."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bo Hazard - April's Fool"
msgstr ""

msgid "December Never Stood a Chance"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load delivered in the dead of winter, heater roaring. You kept rolling."
msgstr ""

msgid "Merle Haggard - If We Make It Through December"
msgstr ""

msgid "All Four Pages of the Calendar"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Deliveries in all four seasons. You've seen the road's whole wardrobe."
msgstr ""

msgid "George Jones - Seasons of My Heart"
msgstr ""

msgid "Through the Furnace Door"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A summer delivery into the desert Southwest, where the door handle bites."
msgstr ""

msgid "Emily Nenni - Gates Of Hell"
msgstr ""

msgid "Every Sky in the Logbook"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You've driven under every sky in the forecast. None of it lasted; you did."
msgstr ""

msgid "Waylon Jennings & Jessi Colter - Storms Never Last"
msgstr ""

msgid "Dark Line on the Radar"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Through a real thunderstorm, and the trailer stayed behind you where it "
"belongs."
msgstr ""

msgid "Channing Wilson - Blues Comin' On"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hot Brakes, Warm Handshake"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On time with almost nothing to spare. The dock tore up the late note."
msgstr ""

msgid "Brennen Leigh & Asleep At The Wheel - Comin' In Hot"
msgstr ""

msgid "Keep the Bonus, Boss"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your first late delivery. The bonus walked, and you learned how much "
"cushion a deadline has."
msgstr ""

msgid "Johnny Paycheck - Take This Job and Shove It"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Small Hours Ride Along"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Freight delivered between midnight and first light. Whatever rode along "
"signed nothing."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dolly Parton & Ben Haggard - Demons"
msgstr ""

msgid "Rolling Before the Roosters"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You pulled out before first light. Early starts pay off in yawns and "
"bonuses."
msgstr ""

msgid "American Aquarium - Waking Up the Echoes"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hope Is Not a Fuel Plan"
msgstr ""

msgid "You made the dock on fumes and prayer. Hope is not a fuel plan."
msgstr ""

msgid "Brennen Leigh - Running Out Of Hope, Arkansas"
msgstr ""

msgid "Vanished Like a Professional"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Over 300 miles, on time, with no damage, strikes, or tickets. The paperwork "
"is your only trace."
msgstr ""

msgid "Caroline Spence - Clean Getaway"
msgstr ""

msgid "Yeah, Officer, That Was Me"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your first speeding ticket, paid at the roadside. Dispatch wasn't even "
"surprised."
msgstr ""

msgid "Drake Milligan - Sounds Like Something I'd Do"
msgstr ""

msgid "Twice in One Trip, Really"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Two speeding tickets in one run. The first was a lesson; the second was a "
"choice."
msgstr ""

msgid "Erin Viancourt - Should've Known Better"
msgstr ""

msgid "Stuck in Every Flavor of Slow"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Cones and a traffic jam on one trip. The truck became a waiting room with "
"mud flaps."
msgstr ""

msgid "Christian Parker - You Ain't Going Nowhere"
msgstr ""

msgid "On a First-Name Basis at the Scale"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Five inspections over your career. You could clear the scale house in your "
"sleep."
msgstr ""

msgid "Caroline Spence - Scale These Walls"
msgstr ""

msgid "Every Box on the Order Sheet"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Every upgrade in the catalog, installed. A fully loaded tractor still turns "
"heads."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dale Watson - Whatever Happened To The Cadillac"
msgstr ""

msgid "Back from the Bottom of the Ledger"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You brought the truck back from 75 percent damage or worse. Only one way to "
"go from there."
msgstr ""

msgid "Alex Williams - Rock Bottom"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Show Rolls On"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Broke down, waited out roadside help, and finished the run. The show rolls "
"on."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dale Watson & Ray Benson - Bus' Breakdown"
msgstr ""

msgid "Regular on the Regional Board"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Career level 5. Dispatch quit double-checking, and you can turn down a load "
"without a lecture."
msgstr ""

msgid "Lead Driver, Says So on the Vest"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Career level 10, senior driver. Better freight, and new hires think you "
"know every dock."
msgstr ""

msgid "Alabama - Forty Hour Week (For a Livin')"
msgstr ""

msgid "Halfway Up the Ladder"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Career level 15. The owner-operator plan is taped to the sun visor now."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dolly Parton - 9 to 5"
msgstr ""

msgid "Qualified for Your Own Numbers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Career level 25. You qualify for your own operating authority. In freight, "
"that's arriving."
msgstr ""

msgid "Waylon Jennings - Are You Sure Hank Done It This Way"
msgstr ""

msgid "All the Way to the Top Rung"
msgstr ""

msgid "Career level 30, the top rung. The road ahead is yours to choose."
msgstr ""

msgid "Newer Iron from the Yard"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dispatch gave you a newer tractor, fueled and washed. Seniority smells like "
"fresh upholstery."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dale Watson - Truckin' Man"
msgstr ""

msgid "First Pick of the Yard"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The fleet flagship, with the big bunk. The yard hands you the keys first."
msgstr ""

msgid "Red Sovine - Phantom 309"
msgstr ""

msgid "A Yard of Your Own"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Three tractors with your name on the titles. The insurance folder calls it "
"a fleet."
msgstr ""

msgid "Kathy Mattea - Eighteen Wheels and a Dozen Roses"
msgstr ""

msgid "Your Name on the Title"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You leased on as an owner-operator. Bigger revenue, your bills, your calls."
msgstr ""

msgid "Running Under Your Own Numbers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your own authority is active. Your freight, your rates, your risk, and all "
"the upside."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hank Williams Jr. - A Country Boy Can Survive"
msgstr ""

msgid "Paid for the Classroom Yourself"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You paid for an endorsement course yourself. Ambition has tuition, and you "
"paid cash."
msgstr ""

msgid "Aaron Tippin - Working Man's Ph.D."
msgstr ""

msgid "Twenty-Five Pins in the Map"
msgstr ""

msgid "Deliveries in 25 cities. The atlas falls open to the right page now."
msgstr ""

msgid "Seventy-Five Docks Deep"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Seventy-five cities have signed for your freight, and the coffee's bad in "
"every one."
msgstr ""

msgid "Willie Nelson - Still Is Still Moving to Me"
msgstr ""

msgid "Half the Map, Signed For"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A hundred fifty cities delivered. The far side of the map is feeling left "
"out."
msgstr ""

msgid "Alan Jackson - Drive (For Daddy Gene)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Fifteen State Lines Behind You"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Freight delivered in 15 states. The glovebox is mostly toll receipts."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bobby Bare - 500 Miles Away from Home"
msgstr ""

msgid "Thirty States and Counting"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Thirty states delivered. Most folks need a camper and a lifetime to see "
"that much."
msgstr ""

msgid "Johnny Cash - Ride This Train"
msgstr ""

msgid "Freight for the High Plains"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load into the Dakotas, where the horizon talks and the wind argues back."
msgstr ""

msgid "Corb Lund - Long Gone to Saskatchewan"
msgstr ""

msgid "Under the Biggest Sky"
msgstr ""

msgid "Freight in Montana, where the radio runs out and the sky doesn't."
msgstr ""

msgid "Merle Haggard - Big City"
msgstr ""

msgid "Down East with a Dry Van"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Into northern New England: narrow bridges, frost heaves, and town names "
"that fight the GPS."
msgstr ""

msgid "Still Proud in Muskogee"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load into Muskogee, Oklahoma. Clean paperwork counts as manners here."
msgstr ""

msgid "Merle Haggard - Okie From Muskogee"
msgstr ""

msgid "Brighter Than the Local TV Star"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Freight into Kansas City. Burnt ends, wide boulevards, and no help backing "
"into the dock."
msgstr ""

msgid "Roger Miller - Kansas City Star"
msgstr ""

msgid "However You Got to Memphis"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Freight in Memphis, where the river hauls nearly as much as the highway."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tom T. Hall - That's How I Got to Memphis"
msgstr ""

msgid "Cold Bay, Warm Welcome"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A delivery into Saginaw, where the bay wind finds every gap in the cab."
msgstr ""

msgid "Lefty Frizzell - Saginaw, Michigan"
msgstr ""

msgid "Cowtown Crossed Your Mind"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load into Fort Worth. The stockyards went showbiz; the freight stayed "
"honest."
msgstr ""

msgid "George Strait - Does Fort Worth Ever Cross Your Mind"
msgstr ""

msgid "Backing Down to San Antone"
msgstr ""

msgid "Freight in San Antonio. The river walks; your trailer rolled."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bob Wills & His Texas Playboys - New San Antonio Rose"
msgstr ""

msgid "Good Morning, Crescent City"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load into New Orleans, a little behind the beat. The coffee fixed it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Willie Nelson - City of New Orleans"
msgstr ""

msgid "One Day Closer, Says the Odometer"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Freight into Houston, sprawling enough for four rush hours. Every mile "
"counted."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Larry Gatlin & The Gatlin Brothers - Houston (Means I'm One Day Closer to "
"You)"
msgstr ""

msgid "A Corner Worth Standing On"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load into Winslow, Arizona. You're the second most photographed thing on "
"the corner."
msgstr ""

msgid "Eagles - Take It Easy"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quicker Than the Old Express"
msgstr ""

msgid "Freight into Chattanooga, quicker than any old train on a schedule."
msgstr ""

msgid "Glenn Miller - Chattanooga Choo Choo"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Jackson Everybody Sings About"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load into Jackson. Tennessee or Mississippi, this badge takes either."
msgstr ""

msgid "Johnny Cash & June Carter - Jackson"
msgstr ""

msgid "Prettiest Town on the Manifest"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Freight into Abilene. The song got there first, but the load needed a truck."
msgstr ""

msgid "George Hamilton IV - Abilene"
msgstr ""

msgid "Somewhere in the Static"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You rode a station to the edge of its reach, until the hill got in the way."
msgstr ""

msgid "Harry Chapin - W.O.L.D."
msgstr ""

msgid "Skip on the Far End"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You caught a station far outside its range, up where the air is thin."
msgstr ""

msgid "Wall of Voodoo - Mexican Radio"
msgstr ""

msgid "Same Song, Three State Lines"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One station carried you across three states. The transmitter's still trying."
msgstr ""

msgid "Golden Earring - Radar Love"
msgstr ""

msgid "Worked the Whole Dial"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Twenty-five stations found and left behind. You're reading the country off "
"the dial."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Carpenters - Yesterday Once More"
msgstr ""

msgid "Down the Mountain on the Jake"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Two miles of real downgrade without touching the service brake. The engine "
"brake held it all."
msgstr ""

msgid "C.W. McCall - Black Bear Road"
msgstr ""

msgid "Smoke, Smoke, Smoke Those Drums"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You cooked the brakes until they started to fade. Next hill, pick a lower "
"gear."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tex Williams - Smoke! Smoke! Smoke! (That Cigarette)"
msgstr ""

msgid "No Mountain High Enough"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Cruise read the hill ahead, banked a little speed, and carried it over the "
"top."
msgstr ""

msgid "Marvin Gaye & Tammi Terrell - Ain't No Mountain High Enough"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sipping It All the Way"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A whole run at better than 8 miles per gallon. Light foot, right gear."
msgstr ""

msgid "Eddie Rabbitt - Drivin' My Life Away"
msgstr ""

msgid "Whatever the Yard Has Free"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Five different tractors under you. You know which spares pull and which "
"just make noise."
msgstr ""

msgid "Every Rung of the Yard"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You've driven every tier of the fleet, trainer rig to first pick. The good "
"iron was worth the wait."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hard Candy Christmas Run"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load signed for on Christmas Day. Somewhere, dinner went on without you."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dolly Parton - Hard Candy Christmas"
msgstr ""

msgid "Superstition, Signed For"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Delivered on Friday the 13th without a scratch. Bad luck took the day off."
msgstr ""

msgid "Stevie Wonder - Superstition"
msgstr ""

msgid "Working Through the Countdown"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Midnight on New Year's, between two towns. They counted down; you counted "
"mile markers."
msgstr ""

msgid "U2 - New Year's Day"
msgstr ""

msgid "And Five Hundred More"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One dispatch over a thousand miles. The weather changed its mind twice."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Proclaimers - I'm Gonna Be (500 Miles)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Never Fought the Law"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fifty deliveries without a ticket. No story to tell, and that's the point."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Bobby Fuller Four - I Fought the Law"
msgstr ""

msgid "Night Moves on the Interstate"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Ten loads delivered in the small hours. Empty lanes and surprised receivers."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bob Seger - Night Moves"
msgstr ""

msgid "One More Cup for the Road"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Twenty-five breaks taken right. The sitting down did more than the coffee."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bob Dylan - One More Cup of Coffee"
msgstr ""

msgid "Drop It and Hook It"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your first drop and hook. You were rolling before a dock could find you a "
"door."
msgstr ""

msgid "Red Sovine - Giddyup Go"
msgstr ""

msgid "You Get What You Get"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You hooked a yard trailer and found a defect on the walk-around. Now it's "
"yours."
msgstr ""

msgid "Send It Back"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You found what was wrong with a trailer and refused it. Thirty minutes for "
"the swap."
msgstr ""

msgid "Leave It Where It Lies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your first drop at the receiver. Leave the loaded trailer, hook an empty, "
"and roll."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Band - The Weight"
msgstr ""

msgid "Somebody Else's Turn"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You hauled a written-up trailer across the country and left it in the "
"receiver's yard. You checked the lights at every stop."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hank Williams - Move It On Over"
msgstr ""

msgid "Paid to Sit Still"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A shipper held you past free time, and the carrier billed them. The clock "
"worked for you."
msgstr ""

msgid "Otis Redding - (Sittin' On) The Dock of the Bay"
msgstr ""

msgid "Summer of Sixty-Nine"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Exactly 69 miles per hour for a full mile. No significance. You know what "
"you did."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bryan Adams - Summer of '69"
msgstr ""

msgid "Where We're Going, We Need Roads"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"88 miles per hour in a loaded truck. No time travel, just a brief lapse in "
"judgment."
msgstr ""

msgid "Huey Lewis and the News - The Power of Love"
msgstr ""

msgid "Another Day Older"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sixteen tons in one load. And what did you get? A sore back and a "
"dispatcher asking for more."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tennessee Ernie Ford - Sixteen Tons"
msgstr ""

msgid "One More for the Ditch"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"After midnight, on fumes, in the rain, and still on time. Nothing went "
"wrong fast enough to matter."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tom Waits - One for My Baby (and One More for the Road)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Wrong Game, No Limit"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Not the mid-90s anymore, whatever Jim Kitchen told you in Trucker. Wrong "
"game. Floor it and hit 88."
msgstr ""

msgid "Sammy Hagar - I Can't Drive 55"
msgstr ""

msgid "Copy That, October"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load settled on the fourth of October, ten-four day. A white knight "
"started it, and the whole channel said it back."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cledus Maggard and the Citizen's Band - The White Knight"
msgstr ""

msgid "Somebody Said Thank You"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A load during Truck Driver Appreciation Week. Doughnuts at the window and a "
"thank-you from dispatch."
msgstr ""

msgid "Andrew Gold - Thank You for Being a Friend"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Classmate Came Back"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Lou turned up as your co-driver, back from Meridian Freight Lines with a "
"story nobody quite believes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Thin Lizzy - The Boys Are Back in Town"
msgstr ""

msgid "Teacher in the Sleeper"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Ray, who ran your training class, rode one load with you to see how you "
"turned out."
msgstr ""

msgid "Jethro Tull - Teacher"
msgstr ""

