msgid "corridor"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Original parody of a well-known Texas travel-center chain that bans big "
"rigs; names and products are invented to keep the joke and drop the mark."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The sign over the entrance is not subtle: no eighteen-wheelers. Big Buck's "
"turns away anything pulling a trailer."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A grinning beaver on a billboard waves you off. No eighteen-wheelers, "
"partner. Not today, not ever."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You will never fit a trailer in that car lot. Drop your trailer somewhere "
"and roll back in bobtail -- just the tractor, no trailer -- and the beaver "
"will let you slip in."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Still hauling a trailer. The greeter's smile is getting thin. You know the "
"rule by now."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"That is three strikes' worth of trailer. A manager in a beaver cap is "
"watching you idle at the entrance."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Last warning: keep blocking the entrance with that rig and Big Buck's will "
"ask you not to come back for a while."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"That does it. The beaver has had enough. You are banned from Big Buck's for "
"a while, and word gets around -- your reputation takes a hit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The greeter recognizes your rig from the entrance camera and shakes his "
"head. Still banned. Come back when things have cooled off."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Five buses of middle-school thrill-seekers are raiding the fudge counter. "
"Maybe give it a pass for now."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A tour bus just unloaded forty road-trippers into the brisket line. Give it "
"an hour."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is a summer Saturday and the lot is packed to the beaver's whiskers. "
"Come back when it is calmer."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Three motor homes, a car club, and a wedding party in the parking lot. No "
"room even for a bobtail today."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"They are restocking the jerky wall and half the pumps are coned off. Swing "
"back later."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The famous restrooms have a line out the door. Trust us -- come back."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Welcome to Big Buck's. Acres of gleaming fuel islands you are not allowed "
"to use, the cleanest restrooms in three counties, and a wall of brisket "
"that can be smelled from the interstate."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You ease the bobtail tractor between two minivans and a beaver the size of "
"a refrigerator waves hello. You made it in."
msgstr ""

msgid "a brisket sandwich the size of a hubcap"
msgstr ""

msgid "Beaver Bites -- glazed corn-nut things that are dangerously good"
msgstr ""

msgid "a slab of homemade fudge from the fudge counter"
msgstr ""

msgid "a foot of house-smoked jerky off the jerky wall"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the Bladder Buster -- a sixty-four-ounce soda cup you could bathe a puppy in"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the Iron Bladder -- premium road briefs for the driver who refuses to stop, "
"priced like they know you have no choice"
msgstr ""

msgid "a souvenir tee that says I Survived Big Buck's"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Original parody billboard copy evoking real interstate roadside culture; "
"real attraction names used nominatively, ad text invented."
msgstr ""

msgid "Did you eat today? Thank a trucker."
msgstr ""

msgid "Last real coffee for two hundred miles. This is not a drill."
msgstr ""

msgid "Prime rib buffet, nine ninety-nine. Cardiologist not included."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hitchhikers may be escaping inmates. Drive friendly."
msgstr ""

msgid "Home of the fifty-pound cinnamon roll. Bring a friend. Bring two."
msgstr ""

msgid "Gun show and craft fair this weekend. Something for everyone."
msgstr ""

msgid "You are now leaving the middle of nowhere. Come back soon."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Big Bob's Burgers: burgers so big, the Department of Transportation "
"requires a second trailer."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Mamma's Diner: home cooking! Because apparently your home doesn't have a "
"kitchen."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Last Chance Cafe: 37 miles back was The First Chance Cafe."
msgstr ""

msgid "World's 3rd-best pie: we used to be #2. Then Jerry complained."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Uncle Josh's Steakhouse: steaks so tender they're legally considered "
"missing."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Next exit: biggest pancake in the state! Probably. We haven't checked."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Free coffee! With purchase of coffee. Extra refills fifty cents each."
msgstr ""

msgid "Next exit: homemade jerky and a gift shop that sells the same jerky."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We have ice. We have bait. We have opinions about your bumper sticker."
msgstr ""

msgid "Diesel, showers, and a fried pie that will change your itinerary."
msgstr ""

msgid "All-you-can-eat catfish. Bring a bigger belt."
msgstr ""

msgid "World's largest frying pan. Breakfast is served. Bring a forklift."
msgstr ""

msgid "Homemade pie, next exit. Made this morning. The coffee is older."
msgstr ""

msgid "Fresh peaches, next exit. Pick your own or grab a bag."
msgstr ""

msgid "Antiques and ammunition. One building. Two hobbies."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you lived here, you'd be home by now. Nobody lives here."
msgstr ""

msgid "Truck wash, next exit. Your trailer used to be white."
msgstr ""

msgid "The coffee is fine. The pie is better. The gossip is unbeatable."
msgstr ""

msgid "Concrete deer and yard gnomes, next exit. We help you load them."
msgstr ""

msgid "Gift shop, next exit. Dashboard hula girls, half off."
msgstr ""

msgid "Local honey. Local jam. Local opinions, free with every purchase."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The steak is bigger than the plate. The plate is bigger than your budget."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Next exit: homemade ice cream. The cows are local. The freezer is older "
"than you."
msgstr ""

msgid "Gun show this weekend, craft fair the next. Same tent."
msgstr ""

msgid "Buffet: if it isn't on a steam table, it isn't dinner."
msgstr ""

msgid "Fireworks, fireworks, fireworks. You're already past it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fireworks barn, next exit. If you can still hear, you haven't shopped "
"enough."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Family fireworks. Professional regret. Open till the sheriff gets here."
msgstr ""

msgid "Buy one crate, get the ringing in your ears free."
msgstr ""

msgid "Stand back. Light fuse. That's the whole business plan. Next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Roman candles, bottle rockets, and a very optimistic fire extinguisher."
msgstr ""

msgid "Closed on Christmas. Open on every other bad idea."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fireworks warehouse. No smoking. We are serious. Look at the inventory."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your brother-in-law already bought the loud ones. Catch up, next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid "World's largest pecan. You'll smell it before you see it. Next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Pecan logs, pecan pie, pecan everything. Your passenger will complain. Buy "
"two."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If it isn't pecans, it isn't a gift. Next exit, we will not be argued with."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"World's second-largest pecan. The biggest one is three exits back and they "
"know it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Fresh roasted pecans. The sample is free. The bag is not."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Pecan pralines, next exit. Sticky steering wheels since nineteen fifty."
msgstr ""

msgid "Nuts. We sell them. We attract them. Next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid "Pecan brittle so hard it needs a load rating."
msgstr ""

msgid "Adult superstore, next exit. Truckers welcome. We will not tell."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Adult bookstore, next exit. Magazines you will not read. Parking you will "
"use."
msgstr ""

msgid "Eighteen and over. Eighteen wheels preferred. Next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The sign just says Superstore. You already know which one. Next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Late night, well lit, no questions. Your logbook does not need this stop."
msgstr ""

msgid "Adult gifts, next exit. For someone else, obviously."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the billboard is this vague, the store is not. Next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Gentleman's club, next exit. Cold beer. Warm welcome. Dispatch stays "
"outside."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"XXX theater, next exit. Dark room. Cheap seats. Nobody looking at you."
msgstr ""

msgid "Open all night. Cash if you prefer. Adult superstore, next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Adult bookstore, next exit. The back room is in the back. You already knew."
msgstr ""

msgid "No cover for truckers. Cover your tracks yourself. Next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid "Feature starts when you sit down. Adult theater, next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid "We sell what the other stores will not name. Superstore, next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid "Your CB will not mention this stop. Adult superstore, next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Last chance before morning. Gentleman's club, next exit. Last call is "
"whenever."
msgstr ""

msgid "Locked cabinet. Open mind. Adult bookstore, next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid "Couples welcome. Couples optional. Next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid "Big lot. Tall doors. Adult superstore. You will fit."
msgstr ""

msgid "Continuous shows. Discreet exits. XXX theater, next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid "Stage is small. Tips are not. Gentleman's club, next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Come for the magazines. Leave with a bag you will hide. Bookstore, next "
"exit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"AM radio, this hour: farm report, funeral notices, and a song you forgot "
"you loved."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Gospel hour on the local AM. The preacher is selling a tent, not a "
"timeshare."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your local station: three songs, two ads, and a birthday shout-out for "
"someone named Dale."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Classic country all night. We play the hits and the ones the hits replaced."
msgstr ""

msgid "AM trucking radio. Static included at no extra charge."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The station that plays only driving songs. You are the whole audience."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tune us in. Tune the other guy out. All request, no sleep."
msgstr ""

msgid "Overnight trucker radio. Road reports and old country till sunrise."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ten thousand watts of somebody's uncle with a stack of records."
msgstr ""

msgid "If your radio still has a knob, we still have a tower."
msgstr ""

msgid "Weather, crop reports, and a hymn at sunrise. You know the station."
msgstr ""

msgid "All truck, all night, all the same three commercials."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Keep it here. The next station is somebody's talk show and a car dealership."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Love's ahead. Diesel, a shower, and a coffee that will keep you legal for "
"one more state."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Pilot next exit. Parking if you are lucky. Coffee if you are desperate."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Travel center: showers, diesel, and a gift shop selling hats you already "
"own."
msgstr ""

msgid "Motel vacancy. Free ice. Free Wi-Fi. Free regret about the mattress."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Chain hotel, next exit. Continental breakfast starts when the waffle iron "
"wakes up."
msgstr ""

msgid "Burger drive-thru, next exit. The bag is small. The line is not."
msgstr ""

msgid "Exit food: burgers, fries, and a soda the size of a fuel can."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Truck parking and a sit-down special. The special is that they still have "
"parking."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sheetz next exit. Made-to-order, open late, and somehow always has a line."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Wawa, next exit. Hoagies, coffee, and a parking lot that thinks it is a "
"city."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"RaceTrac next exit. Fuel, drinks, and a bathroom you will actually use."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Cracker Barrel, next exit. Rocking chairs out front, biscuits inside."
msgstr ""

msgid "Now showing: a movie about a truck. You are living the sequel."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Coming soon to the drive-in: a movie about a truck. You've seen the real "
"thing."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Weekend double feature at the drive-in. Windows up if it rains. Windows "
"down if it smells."
msgstr ""

msgid "Now playing: something with explosions. Popcorn is extra."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Coming Friday: the one with the car chase. Please do not practice on this "
"interstate."
msgstr ""

msgid "Matinee special. Matinee is when you should be sleeping. We know."
msgstr ""

msgid "Streaming now, and somehow also on a billboard. Eyes on the road."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Now showing: a comedy about a road trip. You already know how it ends."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Coming soon: a documentary about highways. You could have narrated it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Drive-in movies, weekends only. Two features for one ticket."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Injured in a truck wreck? Not this trip, we hope. But remember Big Jim."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One call, that's all. Big Jim Tolliver, attorney at law and bass fisherman."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hurt on the job? Big Jim gets you paid. Big Jim gets Big Jim paid more."
msgstr ""

msgid "Eighteen wheels of justice. Big Jim sues trucks. Awkward, we know."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Big Jim, attorney. He's got as many problems as pounds, so he gets yours. "
"Life broke you? He'll sue whoever."
msgstr ""

msgid "Big Jim saw that lane change. He is not mad. He is drafting."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rollover? Call Big Jim. He answers on the first ring."
msgstr ""

msgid "Big Jim Tolliver: because your insurance company has a lawyer too."
msgstr ""

msgid "Whiplash? Big Jim has a cousin who had that. Call him anyway."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Big Jim does not sleep. Big Jim's paralegal does not sleep. The bill does "
"not sleep."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hurt? Not your fault? Big Jim agrees, and he has not even met you."
msgstr ""

msgid "Big Jim's number is on the next six boards. You will remember it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Work injury? Big Jim used to drive. Now he sues the people who do."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Big Jim. Not the other Jim. The billboard Jim. Write it on the visor."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the other guy had a lawyer, you would want Big Jim."
msgstr ""

msgid "Jesus is watching. So is the weigh station. Slow down."
msgstr ""

msgid "Where will you spend eternity? Smoking or non-smoking?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Got God? Give him a try, he'll ride shotgun or side saddle with ya any day "
"or night"
msgstr ""

msgid "Honk if you love the Lord. Text and drive if you'd like to meet him."
msgstr ""

msgid "God answers knee-mail."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A missed exit is not a sign from God. The next weigh station might be."
msgstr ""

msgid "Pray for travelers. Then use your turn signal."
msgstr ""

msgid "Church bake sale, next exit. Salvation and a cookie, in that order."
msgstr ""

msgid "God is good. The coffee at the next truck stop is merely adequate."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Don't make me come down there. Signed, God. Also your safety director."
msgstr ""

msgid "This is your sign. The actual church is the next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid "Sunday service, seven in the morning. The doughnuts go first."
msgstr ""

msgid "Eternity is a long haul. Pack accordingly."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Blessed are the peacemakers, and the folks who stay out of the left lane."
msgstr ""

msgid "Got faith? Keep both hands on the wheel anyway."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mystery Spot ahead. Gravity is a suggestion here. Nine ninety-five."
msgstr ""

msgid "See the two-headed rattlesnake. Alive-ish. Next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid "Alligator farm and fudge shop. Yes, the same building."
msgstr ""

msgid "Living through chemistry, get your chemistry fix next four exits."
msgstr ""

msgid "Zoo! Visit the animals or be one!"
msgstr ""

msgid "See the albino alligator. He is on break. The gift shop is not."
msgstr ""

msgid "Gravity hill ahead. Your truck already knew."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mystery house. Crooked floors. Straight prices. Nine ninety-five."
msgstr ""

msgid "Live rattlesnakes. Dead air conditioning. Next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cave tours, next exit. The crystals in the gift shop are glass."
msgstr ""

msgid "Two-headed calf, stuffed. One-headed cashier, not. Next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid "See the thing in a jar. We will not say which jar. Nine dollars."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Miniature village, next exit. Your rig will not fit down Main Street."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tornado museum, next exit. Step inside the storm cellar."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Tired of driving? Pull over. Take a nap. Your dispatcher will still be mad."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your truck deserves better. You deserve a raise. Neither is happening here."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We buy used trucks! Even the ones that sound like a washing machine full of "
"rocks."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Truckers welcome! Trucks less welcome. Our parking lot only has 6 spaces."
msgstr ""

msgid "Need diesel? Of course you do. $4.89/gallon. Please cry inside."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rest easy at the Budget Palace! Luxury not included."
msgstr ""

msgid "Showers with actual hot water. We are as surprised as you are."
msgstr ""

msgid "Truck parking, next exit. One spot left, behind the dumpster."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Diesel and a hot dog that's been on the roller grill since Tuesday. Next "
"exit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We put out cones for truck parking. Cars park in them anyway. Next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tire shop that does not flinch at your recaps. Next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bugs on the windshield? Free squeegee with every fill-up. Next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"CB shop, next exit. New antennas, and a guy who will talk your ear off."
msgstr ""

msgid "Reefer repair. If it is warm, we can tell from here."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The lot has spaces. They are occupied by people who said they would only be "
"a minute."
msgstr ""

msgid "Fuel desk open all night. The smile closes at ten."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Need a shower, a stall, and a twenty-minute lie-down. We can do two of "
"those."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We buy wrecks, runners, and whatever is smoking behind you. Cash today."
msgstr ""

msgid "Congratulations! You have driven past another billboard."
msgstr ""

msgid "Don't like this billboard? Keep driving."
msgstr ""

msgid "Wall Drug. Five-cent coffee since your grandfather was your age."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Cleveland ahead. The Rock and Roll Hall of Fame sits on the lake. Chuck "
"Berry, Aretha Franklin, and a glass pyramid you can actually visit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Boston ahead. The Willis Brothers needed forty acres to turn a rig around "
"in this town. It hasn't gotten any wider."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Wyoming, Land of the Buffalo. Chancey Williams sings it from right up the "
"road. Buffalo cross wherever they please."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Idaho panhandle country. Colby Acuff and the Western White Pines both grew "
"up here."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Mitchell, South Dakota -- the Corn Palace is a real building they "
"redecorate with corn. You may look. The pigeons already did."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Minnesota. The Spam Museum is a real place they built for a canned lunch. "
"Samples included. The trailer is not."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Bubba's Fireworks: open 362 days a year! Closed on the other three because "
"we're usually in the hospital."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"New Jersey: more state than it gets credit for. Elle King sings one called "
"Jersey Giant."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Jacksonville ahead, hometown of Lynyrd Skynyrd. Down here even the breeze "
"plays guitar -- listen to their Call Me the Breeze."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Virginia peanuts, next exit. Cooked in the shell. Your cab will smell like "
"a ballpark for a week."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Phoenix ahead, eventually. The desert gave us By the Time I Get to Phoenix."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Houston ahead. Larry Gatlin measured this trip in days and just called the "
"song Houston."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Houston ahead. Gilley's, the Urban Cowboy honky-tonk, stood in Pasadena "
"until the eighties. The bull moved to Dallas. The boots stayed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Baton Rouge ahead. Kris Kristofferson set Me and Bobby McGee hitchhiking "
"out of here. Pick up the song, not the hitchhikers."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Biloxi by two? Only if you keep it moving. Ellis Bullard makes it sound "
"easy."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"El Paso, out past the haze. Marty Robbins sang El Paso City and the Streets "
"of Laredo. West Texas gave him the material."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Big Thicket, off to the north -- deep pines and deeper voices. George "
"Jones grew up in there. Welcome to Possum country."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"San Antonio ahead. Fiesta in the spring, Tejano all year. The Alamo does "
"not take eighteen-wheelers."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"New Orleans ahead. Preservation Hall still sells a seat for the jazz. Leave "
"the trailer off the Quarter."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Cajun country. Boudin, cracklins, and a drive-thru that does not need a "
"window. Next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Mad Greek. Gyros in the middle of the Mojave. Trust the desert."
msgstr ""

msgid "Las Vegas ahead. Elvis said Viva. The lights are on all night."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Las Vegas ahead. Another casino, another buffet bigger than your trailer. "
"The odds are not."
msgstr ""

msgid "Historic Route sixty-six. Get your kicks, then get back on schedule."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Historic Route Sixty-Six, right under your wheels. Bobby Troup gave it a "
"song and half the country followed. The old road still takes visitors."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Winslow, Arizona, home of the world-famous corner. The Eagles sang Take It "
"Easy about it, so the town built a park. Statue included."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Memphis, on down the road. Every highway in Tennessee gets there "
"eventually. Tom T. Hall named his route That's How I Got to Memphis."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Memphis ahead. Graceland is a real house with a real ticket line. Elvis "
"lived there. The jumpsuits are in the museum."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Oklahoma City ahead. Casino billboards outnumber the cattle. You have been "
"warned."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Okemah, Oklahoma. Home of Woody Guthrie. This Land Is Your Land. This "
"billboard is somebody else's."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"East Tennessee, home of Dolly Parton. The Smokies raised her. Nobody's "
"worked a longer shift with a bigger smile."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Memphis. Beale Street still sells a ticket. The freight uses a different "
"door."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Nashville ahead. The Grand Ole Opry still sells a ticket. Bring a song or "
"bring freight. They take both."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Albuquerque ahead. Red chile, green chile, and a sky that does not quit. "
"Fuel up."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One of the world's largest porch swings. Seats eighteen. Zero of them "
"truckers."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Dock of the Bay is at the far end of this road. Otis Redding held the "
"best seat. No parking for trailers."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Reno ahead. Biggest Little City, and the neon starts early. Cash the bonus, "
"not the truck."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Iowa Eighty, the world's largest truck stop, is on this road. Parking is a "
"competitive sport. So is the food court."
msgstr ""

msgid "Have you seen the scenery? Neither has your driver!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Rockies, straight ahead and getting bigger. Joe Walsh saw this view and "
"wrote Rocky Mountain Way."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Kansas City ahead. Roger Miller gave it Kansas City Star, the same year he "
"was King of the Road."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Kansas sky, as advertised. The Oz Museum is a few exits off this road in "
"Wamego. Ruby slippers not required."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Saint Louis ahead. The Gateway Arch is the big one. You may look. The "
"trailer stays on this side of the river."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Meramec-style caverns ahead. Outlaws hid here. So can you, for the price of "
"a ticket."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Franklin County, Missouri, same name as the Franklin County Trucking "
"Company. If you drive, they already wrote your song."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Tulsa ahead. Set your watch to Tulsa Time. Don Williams says it runs a "
"little easier."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tulsa ahead. Casino lights off the right. Don't bet the load."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Saint Louis ahead. Blueberry Hill on Delmar is a real room; Chuck Berry "
"played its Duck Room for years. The duck walk is not a traffic pattern."
msgstr ""

msgid "Abbott, Texas -- Willie Nelson's hometown. He's on the road again."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Waco ahead. Croy and the Boys wrote Don't Let Me Die in Waco. The city "
"would like everyone to relax."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Austin ahead. Dale Watson territory -- honky-tonk for people who read weigh "
"station signs."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"San Antonio, down the road. Western swing was born in Texas and Bob Wills "
"drove it. New San Antonio Rose still blooms."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Laredo ahead. Tejano on the AM and the river just south. Keep the "
"accordion, skip the sightseeing detour."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"San Antonio ahead. Tejano weekend on the AM. Conjunto is a dance hall and "
"this highway."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Oklahoma City ahead. Native casino country. The boards started a hundred "
"miles ago."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fort Worth ahead. Billy Bob's Texas is a real honky-tonk with a zip code. "
"Bob Wills already got the other board."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dallas ahead. The Longhorn Ballroom, built for Bob Wills, is open again. "
"Freight to the dock, not the dance floor."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Waco ahead. West, Texas, is kolache country. The bakery has been stopping "
"traffic since the interstate was new."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Flat Kansas: wheat, sky, and telephone poles. Wichita Lineman was about a "
"man up one of these."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Minneapolis ahead. The Mall of America is just south of town in "
"Bloomington, with a roller coaster under the roof. The parking ramps were "
"not built for trailers."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Bakersfield Sound country. Buck Owens and Merle Haggard tuned it, Red "
"Simpson trucked it, Dwight Yoakam kept it running. Turn it up."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Redwood country, far off this road: trees taller than your rig is long. "
"Andrew Gabbard wrote one called Redwood."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Seattle ahead. The museum of pop culture is the colorful blob by the "
"Needle. Jimi Hendrix is inside; the rain is not."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Bakersfield. The Bakersfield Sound still plays. The freight just passes "
"through."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Arkansas Delta bottomland. Johnny Cash grew up picking cotton out here in "
"Dyess. Hold your lane and walk the line."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The old rail line to New Orleans runs this same stretch. Willie Nelson sang "
"the City of New Orleans down it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Alabama, Hank Williams's home state. Move It On Over -- he meant the dog, "
"but the left lane applies."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Birmingham by eight thirty in the morning? It's been done. Andrea and Mud "
"wrote a song about it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Nashville ahead, where a songwriter waits ten years for one hit. Curtis "
"Grimes wrote Ten Year Town about the wait."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Nashville, Music City. The Ryman Auditorium is the mother church. Hats off, "
"then back on the interstate."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fort Payne, Alabama -- hometown of the band Alabama. They sang Roll On for "
"every eighteen wheeler on this road."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Detroit City ahead. Bobby Bare sang it for every homesick southerner on the "
"assembly lines up here."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Saginaw, Michigan, up the interstate. Lefty Frizzell made a fishing town "
"famous. The bay is cold."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Macon, Georgia -- the Allman Brothers' town. Southbound never sounded "
"better than it does on this stretch."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Georgia peaches, next few exits. The stands are real. The claims about "
"whose are best are advertising."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Florida citrus, next few exits. The bags are heavy. The claims about fresh "
"are mostly true."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Horse country. The Kentucky Horse Park is a real farm with a Hall of "
"Champions. Your trailer is not invited to the paddock."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Atlanta ahead, Jerry Reed's town. He made hauling freight in a hurry "
"flat-out famous -- East Bound and Down."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Newnan, Georgia raised Alan Jackson. He learned to drive on the back roads "
"out here and wrote Drive about it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Atlanta ahead. Gladys Knight caught the Midnight Train home to it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Chattanooga ahead. The Choo Choo is a real train, parked at the old "
"terminal station. No ticket required."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Wisconsin made Dave Dudley, and Dave Dudley made Six Days on the Road. "
"Every truck stop jukebox since owes him a quarter."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Detroit, the Motown assembly line. Marvin Gaye, Stevie Wonder, and no "
"mountain high enough to slow the freight."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Detroit builds engines, and it built Bob Seger. Night Moves and Turn the "
"Page came off these roads."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Wisconsin. Cheese, really good cheese, and a dairy billboard that has been "
"up since your last inspection."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Milwaukee ahead. The Harley-Davidson Museum is a real building. The bikes "
"inside are not street-legal, and neither is your trailer in the lobby."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Charleston, West Virginia raised Red Sovine, the voice of every ghost rig "
"and truck stop prayer. Give the Phantom the right of way."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Kathy Mattea grew up just down the river. Her big one, Eighteen Wheels and "
"a Dozen Roses, is about the last run before retirement."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hollers ahead: a porch, a banjo, somebody picking. Dirty Grass Soul sang "
"Back to the Holler. Leave the trailer; a holler road can't turn a rig."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Mountain fog ahead, the local specialty. Think Foggy Mountain Breakdown, "
"and use low beams."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Bristol, on the state line. The Birthplace of Country Music Museum is a "
"real hall. Carter Family country starts here."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Eastern Kentucky, where the grass really does look blue. Brit Taylor wrote "
"Kentucky Blue about home."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Coal country. Tennessee Ernie Ford counted Sixteen Tons of it and famously "
"came up broke."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Louisville ahead. They make the bats here. The Louisville Slugger Museum is "
"the giant one you cannot miss."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Nazareth, Pennsylvania, a few exits north. The Weight is about a stranger "
"rolling in looking for a bed. Book ahead."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"West Texas cotton flats made Waylon Jennings. One question -- Are You Sure "
"Hank Done It This Way -- and outlaw country was born."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Somewhere out there is Lubbock, Texas. Mac Davis kept it in his rear view "
"mirror until he missed it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Abilene ahead. George Hamilton the Fourth made the town sound gentle as a "
"Sunday. Watch for crosswinds."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dallas ahead. Gilley's Dallas keeps the original bull from Urban Cowboy. "
"Eight seconds is the ride. The dock appointment is not."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Orlando ahead. The theme parks are off this road and not for freight. Fuel "
"up, look once, keep going."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Houston ahead. Space Center Houston is a real room they flew from. The "
"trailer stays on the planet."
msgstr ""

msgid "Big Buck's. Two hundred sixty-two miles. You can hold it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Potty like a rockstar. One hundred ninety miles to go, superstar."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Restrooms so clean your mother would approve. She'd also ask why you never "
"call."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hold it. Just hold it. We believe in you. Ninety more miles."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The cleanest restrooms in America, and you'll spend the next four hundred "
"miles thinking about them."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Home of the Bladder Buster. Sixty-four ounces. You come out a changed "
"driver."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hello. Is it the beaver you're looking for?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"That billboard was printed upside down on purpose. Made you look. Big "
"Buck's, next exit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A beaver the size of a refrigerator is waving at you. Ninety miles. Wave "
"back."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fresh brisket, a wall of jerky, and Beaver Bites. Ninety miles. Try to "
"think about anything else."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fudge made fresh this morning. Beaver Bites made fresh this morning. Your "
"diet, made yesterday."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Big Buck's ahead. Acres of gleaming fuel islands, and not one of them for "
"you. Drop the trailer and dream."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Big Buck's. The beaver has a restroom. You have a bladder. Race is on. One "
"hundred twenty miles."
msgstr ""

msgid "Kolaches at Big Buck's. You do not know what that is. You will."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The beaver says the coffee is fresh. The beaver says a lot of things. "
"Eighty miles."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Big Buck's jerky wall: taller than your trailer is long. One hundred miles. "
"Stretch."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Cleanest floors in the state. You will take your boots off in the parking "
"lot. You will not."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Beaver nuggets, beaver soda, beaver everything. Your cardiologist has left "
"the group chat."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One hundred forty miles to a bathroom you will photograph. Do not "
"photograph it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Big Buck's: so many snacks the cart needs a CDL. Next few exits, then a few "
"more."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The beaver is judging your fuel choice. Diesel is not on the menu. Drop the "
"trailer."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Big Buck's gift wall. You will buy a shirt. You will wear it ironically. "
"You will mean it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hold it like you mean it. Forty more miles. The beaver believes in you, "
"mostly."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"They have a car wash for cars. They have a dream for you. Big Buck's, keep "
"holding."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hank Snow claimed he'd been everywhere. This mile marker confirms it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The girl on the billboard? Wrong billboard. Del Reeves saw her a few "
"hundred miles back. Eyes on the road."
msgstr ""

msgid "World's largest ball of twine. Bigger than your problems. Probably."
msgstr ""

msgid "World's largest ketchup bottle. French fries not included."
msgstr ""

msgid "Petrified wood, petrified staff, very lively gift shop."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Big Jim felt that one from his office. Whatever you hit back there, one "
"call, that's all."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hit something a few miles back? Big Jim is not saying it was your fault. "
"Big Jim is not saying it wasn't."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"That new dent already has a lawyer. Big Jim Tolliver, attorney at law."
msgstr ""

msgid "Big Jim heard the crunch. Big Jim always hears the crunch."
msgstr ""

msgid "Fresh ticket on the dash? Big Jim reads those for fun."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Big Jim saw the trooper's lights back there. Big Jim sees all the lights. "
"Call Big Jim."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A citation is not the end of the road. It is the start of a phone call to "
"Big Jim."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Parked by an inspector? Big Jim has argued with a few. He lost, but he was "
"loud about it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Big Jim cannot fix your brakes. Big Jim can complain about the inspector, "
"by the hour."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Even the Lord rested on the seventh day. You could try the seventh hour."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open all night: coffee, pie, and a booth soft enough to sleep in. Nobody "
"here will judge you."
msgstr ""

msgid "Your eyelids are heavy, and so is your load. Rest is holy too."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All-night diner. The waitress has seen that face before. It looked more "
"awake then."
msgstr ""

msgid "Sleep is a gift. Unwrap it somewhere legal."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Happy New Year. Your resolution is a clean logbook. Big Jim's resolution is "
"more clients."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"New Year's week. Somewhere a fireworks barn sold out of everything loud, "
"and the dogs are already under the bed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Happy Fourth of July. Somewhere a brother-in-law is lighting the loud ones. "
"Mind the smoke."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Independence week. Flags on every porch, and a grill going in every yard "
"for a thousand miles."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Halloween week. The corn mazes are open, and the scarecrows are judging "
"your lane discipline."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Happy Halloween. The scariest thing on this road is still the weigh station."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Thanksgiving week. Somewhere a turkey is grateful you are hauling freight "
"and not him."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Happy Thanksgiving. Every pie case in the country is full, and every pair "
"of pants is worried."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Merry Christmas. Somewhere a nativity scene has a semi in it this year. It "
"is parked legally."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Big Jim wishes you a merry Christmas. Big Jim still wants you to call."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Christmas week. The freight is presents now, and every dock wants it "
"yesterday."
msgstr ""

