msgid "light"
msgstr ""

msgid "standard"
msgstr ""

msgid "heavy"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The dependable tractor you started with: better fuel economy and a calmer "
"highway feel than the heavy hauler."
msgstr ""

msgid "heavy hauler"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A brute for heavy loads and long stretches: a quarter more torque and a two "
"hundred gallon tank, but blunt aerodynamics and a thirstier engine."
msgstr ""

msgid "trainer day cab"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The tractor every new hire learns on: a plain day cab with soft power, "
"light steering, and nowhere to sleep. Forgiving, slow, and impossible to be "
"precious about."
msgstr ""

msgid "yard mule"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A stubby day cab that spends most of its life shoving trailers around the "
"lot. Grunt down low, no manners above fifty, and it drinks like it is being "
"punished."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A tired flat-roof sleeper handed down the seniority list until it reached "
"you. The bunk is thin and the paint is faded, but it will get you there and "
"back."
msgstr ""

msgid "plain jane conventional"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"No chrome, no fairings, no nonsense: a base-spec conventional sleeper "
"bought by the dozen. Nothing about it is special and nothing about it "
"breaks."
msgstr ""

msgid "city shuttle"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A short, light day cab built for stop-and-go: it turns inside its own "
"trailer, sips diesel in traffic, and leaves every pound it saves for the "
"freight."
msgstr ""

msgid "dock hopper"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The everyday city day cab: enough pull for a full trailer, tight mirrors, "
"and air seats that have seen a thousand docks. Home every night by design."
msgstr ""

msgid "short-haul stubnose"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A heavy-spec day cab for the loads nobody wants on a light tractor: gravel, "
"steel, and drum mixers. All driveline, no comfort, and it will pull a "
"building off its footings."
msgstr ""

msgid "mid-roof runner"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A light mid-roof sleeper for drivers who live on two-day lanes: quick, "
"economical, and just tall enough to stand up and change a shirt."
msgstr ""

msgid "farm road workhorse"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Built for grain country: heavy driveline, tall gearing, and a chassis that "
"shrugs off washboard county roads. It hauls hoppers in spring and complains "
"about it all summer."
msgstr ""

msgid "sunset day cab"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A tidy regional day cab: light, easy on diesel, and happy on short lanes. "
"No bunk, no long-haul pretensions."
msgstr ""

msgid "ridgeline sleeper"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A mid-roof regional sleeper with a little more pull and a bigger tank: the "
"workhorse most fleets hand a proven regional driver."
msgstr ""

msgid "old longnose"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A classic long-hood conventional: strong pull and a proud profile, but it "
"fights the wind and drinks for the privilege."
msgstr ""

msgid "long run mid-roof"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A no-drama mid-roof built for the middle of the country: honest range, "
"honest power, and a bunk you can actually sleep a full ten hours in."
msgstr ""

msgid "dry lightning"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A light-spec aero sleeper that runs the desert lanes: it gives up torque "
"for tare weight and mileage, and it will out-run anything in the yard on "
"flat ground."
msgstr ""

msgid "interstate condo"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A raised-roof sleeper with room to stand, cook, and live: the truck drivers "
"move into rather than drive. Heavy on comfort, steady everywhere else."
msgstr ""

msgid "steel hauler"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A heavy-spec flatbed tractor with a headache rack and a driveline sized for "
"coil and plate. Rides like a brick empty and like it was born to it loaded."
msgstr ""

msgid "mountain spec hauler"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Spec'd for the western grades: deep gearing, a big retarder, and brakes "
"that stay cool where other trucks start smelling hot. Slow up, unbothered "
"down."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A raised-roof long-haul sleeper with a two hundred gallon tank and honest "
"aerodynamics: built to live on the interstate for days at a time."
msgstr ""

msgid "big bunk conventional"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A big-bunk conventional with serious torque for mountain corridors and "
"heavy long-haul freight. Comfortable, capable, and a little thirsty."
msgstr ""

msgid "aero cruiser"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A slippery fleet aero tractor tuned for fuel economy: modest torque, long "
"legs, and the best mileage of the long-haul pool."
msgstr ""

msgid "cabover revival"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A modern cabover: short, light, and startlingly quick, with the whole road "
"laid out under the windshield. Every pound it saves goes to the load, and "
"it turns where nothing else will."
msgstr ""

msgid "chrome shop special"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Every light the catalog sells and a stack of polished pipe: a senior "
"driver's reward truck. It is genuinely good, and it knows exactly how good "
"it looks."
msgstr ""

msgid "deep sleeper custom"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A stretched custom sleeper with a proper bed and a wardrobe: for drivers "
"who are out for a month at a time and have stopped pretending otherwise."
msgstr ""

msgid "wide glide tourer"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A wide-cab highway tourer built around the seat and the sound system: quiet "
"at speed, easy over a long day, and no trouble at all in a crosswind."
msgstr ""

msgid "granite grade king"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A heavy-spec premium tractor for the worst grades on the map: enormous "
"torque, oversized brakes, and a retarder that holds a loaded trailer down a "
"six percent without a word."
msgstr ""

msgid "summit flagship"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A premium flagship sleeper: big power, a two hundred twenty gallon tank, "
"and clean aerodynamics. The truck senior drivers ask the shop about."
msgstr ""

msgid "silver aero"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A polished premium aero tractor: the slipperiest shape in the catalog with "
"plenty of pull, sipping diesel at cruise like a truck half its size."
msgstr ""

msgid "midnight flyer"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A light-spec flagship for drivers who run nights: the quietest cab on the "
"property, a huge tank, and mileage that makes a dispatcher smile."
msgstr ""

msgid "owner spec showpiece"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Ordered the way an owner would order it, then handed to the driver the "
"carrier least wants to lose. Everything on it is the good version."
msgstr ""

msgid "centurion longhood"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A flagship long-hood with a hood you could land a plane on: monstrous "
"torque, brakes to match, and an unapologetic thirst. The truck people "
"photograph at the fuel island."
msgstr ""

msgid "continental expedition"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Built to cross the continent without a scheduled stop: two hundred fifty "
"gallons, mountain-grade brakes, and enough torque to make a loaded pull "
"feel like an errand."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The top of the yard: huge torque, a two hundred forty gallon tank, and "
"brakes that shrug off long mountain descents. First pick goes to the "
"carrier's best."
msgstr ""

msgid "night flag aero"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A flagship aero sleeper for drivers who live out west: enormous range, "
"upgraded brakes, and the lowest drag on the road. It turns fuel islands "
"into scenery."
msgstr ""

msgid "Engine tune"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Gives the truck more pulling power. It helps with heavy freight, hill "
"climbs, mountain grades, and starting from a stop with a load. Buy it when "
"heavy loads and steep routes feel sluggish."
msgstr ""

msgid "Aerodynamic kit"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Makes the truck burn less fuel at highway speed. It does not add more fuel "
"capacity; it makes the same tank last longer. Buy it to save diesel money "
"over long highway miles."
msgstr ""

msgid "Long-range tank"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Adds fifty gallons of fuel capacity. It does not make the truck more "
"efficient; it lets you carry more fuel. Buy it for more distance between "
"fuel stops and more route flexibility."
msgstr ""

msgid "Reinforced brakes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Keeps braking power strong for longer when the brakes get hot. It helps on "
"mountain descents, with heavy freight, and during emergency stops. Buy it "
"when downhill control matters more than speed or range."
msgstr ""

msgid "Headlights West, from Freight Fate 1.5"
msgstr ""

msgid "Open Road, from Freight Fate 1.5"
msgstr ""

msgid "Night Haul, from Freight Fate 1.5"
msgstr ""

