msgid "Lane and steering"
msgstr ""

msgid "The engine lean"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Not a sound of its own: it is the engine you are always hearing, leaning to "
"one side. Steer toward the engine, unless you have set the Steering guide "
"row to steer away from it. It leans the way the wheel should go, so it "
"points into a bend before you reach it and away from the edge you are "
"drifting toward. This is the one cue here you follow rather than avoid, and "
"it eases back to the middle as you make the turn or come straight."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Every bend and street corner, in every lane keeping mode. It also leans to "
"correct drift when lane keeping is partial or off and lane departure "
"warning is on. Silent when the lane guide sound is set to tone, because the "
"tone leans instead. The Steering guide row reverses which way to steer."
msgstr ""

msgid "Where you sit in the lane"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The road noise under the truck, sitting where you are in your lane rather "
"than where you should be going. Drift left and it goes left with you. It is "
"the quieter half of the pair: the engine tells you what to do, this tells "
"you what you have done."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Lane keeping partial or off. On full lane keeping the truck holds the lane "
"for you and the road stays centered."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rumble strip, clipped"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A tire is just catching the edge line on that side. You are still in the "
"lane. Steer gently away from it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Lane keeping partial or off."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rumble strip"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The whole tire is on the rumble strip on that side. Steer away now: the "
"next rung of this ladder is off the pavement."
msgstr ""

msgid "Off the pavement"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Gravel. The truck has left the road surface on that side. Ease back on: do "
"not yank the wheel, and do not brake hard while a trailer wheel is still in "
"the dirt."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Lane keeping partial or off. Past an undivided centerline there is no "
"gravel, so the rumble strip stays the outermost sound and the spoken "
"warning carries the danger."
msgstr ""

msgid "Back in the lane"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The soft chime that says you are centered again. It is the all-clear after "
"a drift, and it also marks a bend taken cleanly when driving speech is set "
"to Urgent only."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The all-clear after a drift needs lane keeping partial or off and "
"lane-departure warning on. The short answer to a bend needs curve callouts "
"on and driving speech set to Urgent only."
msgstr ""

msgid "Lane line crossed"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The tires rolling over the raised markers of a painted line. You have "
"changed lanes, whether you meant to or not. A quieter version of it means "
"you have crossed the same line again straight away."
msgstr ""

msgid "Lane locator"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A soft tock, once a beat, panned to where the truck sits inside its lane. "
"You turn it on and off yourself and it keeps ticking until you stop it. "
"Press I to toggle it. The demo walks it from the left of the lane to the "
"right."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Lane keeping partial or off, above walking pace, and the I-key lane locator "
"switched on."
msgstr ""

msgid "Lane guide tone"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A soft note that leans toward the side to steer and stops when you are "
"straight again. You only hear this if you have switched the lane guide "
"sound from engine to tone; the default is the engine itself leaning, with "
"nothing added."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Lane guide sound set to tone, and lane departure warning on with lane "
"keeping off or partial. The Steering guide row reverses it the same way it "
"reverses the engine."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rumble strip, single hit"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A single hit of rumble strip with nothing held after it. A tired driver "
"wandering, or the truck catching the edge for a moment. If you did not "
"steer, it is fatigue, and it is telling you to find somewhere to stop."
msgstr ""

msgid "Transverse strips"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Grouped bars cut across the whole lane, not along its edge. Real road "
"agencies only cut these ahead of a curve that has killed people. Brake as "
"soon as you hear them; they are placed far enough back that braking still "
"makes the corner."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mechanical blinker"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A turn signal relay: a tick, then a softer tock, at a steady pace. During a "
"full-assist lane change it comes from the side you are moving toward. With "
"lane keeping partial or off, it follows your position within the lane while "
"you steer. Signaling for an exit starts it on the right until you take the "
"ramp, cancel, or miss the exit, even after the exit lane is set. Ordinary "
"steering clicks stop when the move ends, with the blinker clicking off; an "
"assisted lane change ends with the sound of tires crossing the painted line."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The I-key locator silences ordinary steering clicks, but not an armed exit "
"signal."
msgstr ""

msgid "Blinker off"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The turn signal stalk clicking back to the middle, from straight ahead. You "
"hear it when you straighten up after steering over, when the exit lane is "
"set, and when you cancel an exit while its blinker is running. The move is "
"finished."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Straightening up clicks it off only with lane keeping partial or off and "
"the I-key locator off. Canceling a running exit blinker clicks it off in "
"every mode."
msgstr ""

msgid "Signal tone"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A short confirmation tone. It marks a move you meant to make: crossing into "
"another lane, easing onto the shoulder, coming up a ramp, or taking the "
"exit the route asked for. Exit lane readiness is announced separately; the "
"exit blinker continues until the ramp or cancellation."
msgstr ""

msgid "Air and brakes"
msgstr ""

msgid "Air building"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The compressor filling the tanks. The truck cannot move until there is "
"enough air in them, so start the engine, leave the parking brake set, and "
"wait for it to reach a hundred psi."
msgstr ""

msgid "Air dryer purge"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A short sharp pop from under the truck when the tanks reach full and the "
"compressor cuts out. Nothing is wrong; it is the sound of the air system "
"being healthy."
msgstr ""

msgid "Low air buzzer"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Air pressure has fallen too low to brake safely. Stop using the brakes, let "
"the compressor catch up, and keep the parking brake set until it does. Hard "
"repeated braking is what empties the tanks fastest."
msgstr ""

msgid "Parking brake set"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The parking brake going on: a hard mechanical clunk of air dumping. The "
"truck will not move until you release it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Parking brake released"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The parking brake coming off. You are free to roll, which also means the "
"truck can roll on a grade before you are ready."
msgstr ""

msgid "Emergency brake"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The hardest stop the truck has. It is for a hazard you cannot otherwise "
"miss, or a stop you would otherwise overshoot, and it is rough on the load."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tire screech"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The tires have lost their grip on the road. Ease off the brake, throttle or "
"steering, whichever you were using, rather than adding more of it. On a wet "
"or icy road this arrives at speeds that would be fine on dry pavement."
msgstr ""

msgid "Engine brake, speed and shifting"
msgstr ""

msgid "Engine brake, stage one"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Two cylinders of retard: the lightest setting. Enough to hold speed on a "
"gentle grade without touching the brakes. Drivers call this the jake."
msgstr ""

msgid "Engine brake, stage two"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Four cylinders of retard. The usual working setting on a long descent. "
"Drivers call this the jake."
msgstr ""

msgid "Engine brake, stage three"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Six cylinders: everything the engine brake has. Loud enough that towns ban "
"it, which is what a no engine brake zone is about. Drivers call this the "
"jake."
msgstr ""

msgid "Overspeed chime"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You are over the posted limit here. It is not a ticket and nobody has "
"necessarily seen you, but an officer who has will act on it. The faster the "
"chime repeats, the further over you are."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"More than 7 miles per hour over the posted limit: past anything adaptive "
"cruise will do on its own, and short of where a trooper can act on your "
"speed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Gear grind"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The shift did not take. Clutch in properly and try the gear again; grinding "
"wears the box and leaves you without drive on a grade."
msgstr ""

msgid "Manual transmission only."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ramps and stop bars"
msgstr ""

msgid "Stop bar tone"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A continuous tone that means the stop bar is close enough that you must "
"already be stopping. It runs until you have stopped or passed it. Treat it "
"as the last warning, not the first."
msgstr ""

msgid "Stop bar countdown"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Beeps that come faster the closer the stop bar gets. When they run together "
"into the steady tone above, you should already be nearly stopped."
msgstr ""

msgid "Green light"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The signal at the bottom of the ramp is green. You may go through without "
"stopping if you are already rolling."
msgstr ""

msgid "Red light"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The signal has gone red. Stop at the bar and wait for green. Rolling "
"through draws horns; going through at speed means cross traffic hits the "
"trailer."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hazards and the road"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hazard warning"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Something in your path needs a real reaction now: brake below twenty five "
"miles per hour quickly, or move to a clear lane if the warning says the "
"object is in your lane."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hazard clear"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You got past the hazard. This is the success half of the dodge outcome "
"pair: at Urgent only it is the whole confirmation that you cleared it, and "
"you can go back to normal speed. Its opposite is the collision below. The "
"two sound nothing alike, so 'did I make it?' is never in doubt."
msgstr ""

msgid "Collision"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You hit it. This is the failure half of the dodge outcome pair: where the "
"hazard-clear chime says you got past, this says you did not, and a spoken "
"damage figure follows. At Urgent only the sound is the outcome, so it is "
"worth knowing before you need it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Construction zone"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Roadwork ahead. The posted limit drops, a lane may close, and the taper "
"callout names which side. Move over when told or you will go through the "
"barrels."
msgstr ""

msgid "Traffic slowing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The traffic in front of you is coming down in speed. Back off the throttle "
"before you need the brakes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Turn ahead"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A street maneuver is coming on a local drive. The spoken guidance that "
"follows names the street and the direction."
msgstr ""

msgid "Turn left"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The next maneuver is a left. Be under the advised speed before the corner: "
"a loaded trailer off-tracks through a city turn."
msgstr ""

msgid "Turn right"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The next maneuver is a right. Same rule as a left, and a right in a truck "
"needs more room than it looks like it should."
msgstr ""

msgid "State line"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You have crossed into another state. Speed limits and rules can change with "
"it, and the spoken callout names the new state."
msgstr ""

msgid "Toll charged"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A toll gantry or plaza has billed the truck. Tolls are settled at delivery, "
"listed separately from anything you were fined."
msgstr ""

msgid "Yawn"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You are the one making this sound. Fatigue is building, faster at night, "
"and a tired driver drifts and reacts late. Plan a stop rather than pushing "
"through it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Enforcement"
msgstr ""

msgid "Enforcement marker"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A short pair of rising tones, twice over, straight ahead. An enforcement "
"post is about to be close enough to watch you, and this arrives before it "
"can see anything. Be at the limit the moment you hear it: what you do after "
"this tone is all an officer sitting there has to go on."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Always. Nothing turns it off. Every post that is allowed to cost you "
"anything sounds this first, at every enforcement presence setting, and the "
"radio is pulled down out of the way so you can hear it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Police car going by"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The marker again, with a vehicle going past a fifth of a second behind it. "
"You have just passed an enforcement post and a marked car is around it. "
"This one is news, not a warning: it sounds once you are already by, and it "
"does not tell you whether anybody was sitting there. The demo plays it on "
"the left, the side an ordinary post is on, and then on the right, the side "
"a weigh station is on."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Past a post with somebody in it, at any enforcement presence setting. Past "
"an empty one, only with presence set to full. Never past a scale that is "
"being worked: there the approach bed carries the warning instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "Siren"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A trooper is pulling you over. Signal, brake, and stop on the shoulder. "
"Ignoring it is logged as evasion and costs far more than the ticket would "
"have. On the road it starts quiet and grows over the first few seconds as "
"the cruiser comes up behind you; the demo holds one steady level, so the "
"rise is the part you will only hear out there."
msgstr ""

msgid "Inspection warning"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You are being looked at for something other than speed: visible damage, no "
"chains inside a chain control, or following far too close."
msgstr ""

msgid "Scale warning"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An open weigh station is ahead. The full spoken notice, with the distance, "
"name and exit key, follows right behind it. Its own low thump-then-beep, "
"not the inspection cue, so the scale is unmistakable before a word is "
"spoken."
msgstr ""

msgid "Scale green light"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A weigh-in-motion transponder cleared this truck as it approached an open "
"scale: keep rolling, no exit needed. Follows right behind the open-scale "
"notice, never instead of it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A weigh station transponder only. The fleet issues one free at career level "
"4, or an owner-operator can subscribe from Business status. Without one, "
"every open scale still demands every truck pull in."
msgstr ""

msgid "Scale red light"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A weigh-in-motion transponder called this truck in anyway: signal for the "
"scale exit and pull in, the same as any driver without a transponder. "
"Compliant trucks are still red-lighted sometimes, and an overweight load "
"always is."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A weigh station transponder only. The fleet issues one free at career level "
"4, or an owner-operator can subscribe from Business status."
msgstr ""

msgid "Weigh station"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The bed that swells as you come up on an open scale. An open scale must be "
"pulled into; blowing past one is its own stop. On the road it comes up "
"under the engine rather than over it, so it is quieter there than it is "
"here."
msgstr ""

msgid "Spike strip"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The end of a pursuit. If you are hearing this, running from the lights has "
"already gone as badly as it can go."
msgstr ""

msgid "CB chatter"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The squelch of a CB call ending, played with what another driver passed on: "
"enforcement, wrecks, work zones. The report says how sure it is, it is "
"sometimes out of date, and it never claims the road is clear."
msgstr ""

msgid "The load"
msgstr ""

msgid "Surge"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Liquid running back and forth inside a tank trailer. It builds while you "
"brake or accelerate and it pushes the truck after you have stopped doing "
"whatever started it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Liquid bulk freight in a tank trailer only."
msgstr ""

msgid "Surge strike"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The load hitting the front or back of the tank. It shoves the truck along "
"its length, which is why a smooth bore tank is braked early and gently "
"rather than late and hard."
msgstr ""

msgid "Surge strike, sideways"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The load hitting the side of the tank. It has its own voice, separate from "
"the fore-and-aft strike, because it means something different: this is the "
"one that rolls trucks. It arrives after you have already turned or changed "
"lanes."
msgstr ""

msgid "It is an engine and it sounds like one."
msgstr ""

msgid "The same engine, in its earlier sound."
msgstr ""

msgid "As the idle loop: an engine at an engine speed."
msgstr ""

msgid "As the idle loop."
msgstr ""

msgid "An engine starting, immediately after you started it."
msgstr ""

msgid "An engine stopping, immediately after you stopped it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The classic jake sound: the same three staged entries play it when "
"Settings, Audio has Engine brake sound set to classic, through the same "
"key-resolution routing the drive uses. Not a second cue."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rain, wind, snow and thunder name themselves."
msgstr ""

msgid "Scene, not a cue: no decision attached."
msgstr ""

msgid "Songs."
msgstr ""

msgid "Menu feedback, learned in the first ten seconds of the main menu."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Static means weak signal to anyone who has owned a radio, and the station "
"dropping is spoken aloud when it happens."
msgstr ""

msgid "The fringe flutter, same reason as the hiss bed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Plays under a spoken line that already explains it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Pavement seams: texture, not a decision."
msgstr ""

msgid "A door."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The driver window, the wind through it and the fan, right after the key "
"that set them, which says what changed."
msgstr ""

msgid "A fuel pump, at a fuel pump."
msgstr ""

msgid "A backup beeper while backing up."
msgstr ""

msgid "The player is holding the horn key."
msgstr ""

msgid "It means you braked hard, which you know."
msgstr ""

msgid "The air letting off after you released the brake pedal."
msgstr ""

msgid "A gear change in a truck that is changing gear."
msgstr ""

msgid "Banked gear changes, same reason."
msgstr ""

msgid "A vehicle going past sounds like a vehicle going past."
msgstr ""

msgid "As the car pass."
msgstr ""

msgid "A vehicle crossing in front sounds like one."
msgstr ""

msgid "As the car cross."
msgstr ""

msgid "A vehicle near the cab sounds like one, where it is."
msgstr ""

msgid "As the car loop."
msgstr ""

msgid "Distant freeway traffic: texture, not a decision."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ambient bed for a place the game has already named."
msgstr ""

msgid "Menu feedback at a facility, not a road cue."
msgstr ""

