"Roadside billboards, read as you pass them: attorney ads and questionable "
"tourist traps."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {place_callouts}
msgid "Place callouts: {place_callouts}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Place names along the road. Sparse speaks only the town names that explain "
"a speed limit change, like Entering Strawberry before its 35. All adds the "
"towns the route passes. Off silences place names; speed limits are never "
"affected."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {on_off}
msgid "Menu position announcements: {on_off}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On, menus say the position, like 3 of 10, after each option. Off, only the "
"option."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {backup_announcements_label}
msgid "Say when a career is backed up: {backup_announcements_label}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"How often you hear that a career is backed up to your orinks.net account. "
"Every time, after each save. Once a session, the first backup of each "
"career after the game starts. Never keeps it quiet. Backups keep going "
"either way, and a refused backup is always spoken."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {event_voice_label}
msgid "Driving event voice: {event_voice_label}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Road events through the main voice or a separate system voice that "
"VoiceOver cannot cut off. The rate, pitch, volume, and voice rows below "
"appear only when the voice supports them; with VoiceOver running, set those "
"in VoiceOver."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Road events through the main voice or a separate SAPI or OneCore voice a "
"screen reader cannot cut off. The rate, pitch, volume, and voice rows below "
"appear only when the voice supports them; with a screen reader running, set "
"those in the screen reader."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {output_label}
msgid "Output: {output_label}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Speech and braille speaks every line and, with NVDA or JAWS, shows it on "
"your braille display too. Braille only puts every line on the display and "
"speaks nothing: menus, readouts, and road events alike. It needs NVDA or "
"JAWS; with any other voice the game keeps speaking and says so."
msgstr ""

msgid "faster"
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {state}
msgid "JAWS arrow keys: {state}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"JAWS reads each arrow key with its own script, which waits for the screen "
"to change, so menus answer slowly and held arrows lag. Faster adds a small "
"script for this game to your JAWS settings so the arrows answer at once. "
"Default removes it. Restart JAWS if nothing changes."
msgstr ""

