#. placeholders: {pace_label}
msgid "Driving mode: {pace_label}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Pacing and pressure. Relaxed passes about ten minutes of road and clock "
"each real minute, with wider hazard windows, gentler damage and fatigue, "
"calmer speech, and the most time to respond. Standard keeps balanced "
"pressure and moves twice as fast, about twenty minutes each real minute. "
"Real time keeps Standard's pressure and runs the driving clock at the speed "
"of a real clock, lined up with your computer's date and time; delivery time "
"remaining and hours of service do not move. Changeable mid-drive from the "
"pause menu; the new pacing starts when the truck next stops."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {hos_label}
msgid "Hours of service: {hos_label}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Realistic: full hours rules and normal road hazards. Relaxed: the same "
"11-hour drive, 14-hour window, and 30-minute break, with lighter fines, "
"fewer inspections, and rare road hazards."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {else}
msgid "Hours of service planning hints: {else}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Off"
msgstr "Tắt"

msgid "On"
msgstr "Bật"

msgid ""
"Optional early advice for a break or sleep stop with time to spare. If an "
"earlier stop fits, the hint also names the last legally reachable fallback. "
"While rolling, use the Rest control to select the recommended stop; use it "
"again to cancel. Standard driving speech speaks one suggestion before the "
"next hours warning. The driving time readout gives full hours and route "
"details. Quiet and Urgent only keep the automatic hint silent. Your "
"required hours warnings and readout controls still work when this is off. "
"It also reminds you before a chain-law road if you have no chains: on the "
"dispatch board when the load crosses a road where trucks must carry chains "
"this season, or where live weather or a weather alert puts a chain law in "
"effect for your truck, while the terminal garage can still sell you a set, "
"and on the road when a posted chain law requires chains on your truck. It "
"never buys anything."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {else}
msgid "Weather source: {else}"
msgstr ""

msgid "real world"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Real world uses live city conditions when available, and reads the Weather "
"Service's active warnings along your route: dispatch plans around a "
"blizzard, ice storm, hurricane or tornado warning, and the cab reads a "
"warning out as you drive into it."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {else}
msgid "Traffic source: {else}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Real time uses live traffic incidents from state 511 services when "
"available."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {else}
msgid "Fuel prices: {else}"
msgstr ""

msgid "this week's national average"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This week's national average puts the federal weekly diesel survey price at "
"every pump, with each region's usual difference on top. Simulated draws a "
"price per region for the session."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {else}
msgid "Parking source: {else}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Real time uses live truck parking availability from TPIMS when available."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {on_off}
msgid "Live weather controls calendar: {on_off}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On, live weather uses today's real date and season. Off, the career date "
"advances at midnight and seasons pass while weather still comes from the "
"real world."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {on_off}
msgid "Facility streets: {on_off}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On, you drive the real streets between the highway and a facility, turn by "
"turn. Off, as in version 1.8, the exit ramp ends at the facility gate, no "
"exit has a light or stop sign, a loaded run leaves straight onto the "
"highway, and a pickup in town is one stretch of road. Applies from your "
"next drive."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {else}
msgid "Units: {else}"
msgstr ""

