msgid "Fully stopped at a route stop, {control_rest} opens its services."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_rest}
msgid ""
"Fully stopped at a route stop, {control_rest} opens its services. Fully "
"stopped elsewhere, {control_rest} opens the emergency shoulder-sleep "
"warning; nearby route points always take priority."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_rest}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid ""
"Fully stopped elsewhere, {control_rest} opens the emergency shoulder-sleep "
"warning; nearby route points always take priority."
msgstr ""

msgid "Traffic, weather, and enforcement"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"GPS announces state lines, towns, route changes, traffic, work zones, and "
"useful stops. Grades and terrain come from the route; weather and traffic "
"vary by place and time."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "Check before changing lanes or returning after a pass."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "Nearby vehicles merge, slow, pass, and queue."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_lane}
msgid ""
"Nearby vehicles merge, slow, pass, and queue. {control_lane} tells you "
"which neighboring lanes are available. Check before changing lanes or "
"returning after a pass."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_lane}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "{control_lane} tells you which neighboring lanes are available."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A passing vehicle grows louder alongside you, then fades ahead. Listen for "
"which side it is on, but use the lane check before moving over."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Mainline traffic stays to your left on an on-ramp. The distant freeway "
"sound follows traffic activity, so busy and quiet stretches sound different."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Brake now means slow promptly. Change lanes or brake names an available "
"lane. A fixed object needs a near-stop if you cannot change lanes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"No lane open means brake. Full lane keeping can pass slow vehicles, but "
"leaves debris avoidance to you and avoids starting a pass near an exit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Leave a coned lane when warned. Driving through barrels causes damage, a "
"citation, and a serious violation."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "Snow and ice need gentler braking and steering."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid ""
"Weather changes grip, visibility, safe speed, following distance, and fuel "
"use."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_weather}
msgid ""
"Weather changes grip, visibility, safe speed, following distance, and fuel "
"use. {control_weather} reports conditions. Snow and ice need gentler "
"braking and steering."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_weather}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "{control_weather} reports conditions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The calendar starts in spring and advances with driving and rest. Live "
"weather can follow the real date or an independent career calendar."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "Ignoring the lights escalates to a forced stop or pursuit."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_take_exit}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid ""
"When a trooper signals you, use {control_take_exit} and brake to a stop for "
"a license and logbook check."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_take_exit}
msgid ""
"When a trooper signals you, use {control_take_exit} and brake to a stop for "
"a license and logbook check. Ignoring the lights escalates to a forced stop "
"or pursuit."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "CB chatter reports what other drivers saw, with uncertainty."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_cb}
msgid ""
"CB chatter reports what other drivers saw, with uncertainty. It can be "
"stale and never claims the road is clear. {control_cb} repeats it with "
"updated distance."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "It can be stale and never claims the road is clear."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_cb}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "{control_cb} repeats it with updated distance."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Citations cost money and affect your record. Serious violations can suspend "
"your CDL and remove driving work; fleeing is a major offense."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The dash overspeed chime is a free warning. Tickets already paid on the "
"road are not charged again at settlement."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_take_exit}, {control_rest}
msgid ""
"At an open scale, slow into its lane, signal with {control_take_exit}, "
"stop, then use {control_rest} for inspection check-in."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hours, fatigue, and rest stops"
msgstr "Giờ lái xe, mệt mỏi và điểm nghỉ"

msgid ""
"The hours clock permits eleven driving hours after ten hours off, inside a "
"fourteen-hour duty window. A thirty-minute break is due after eight "
"cumulative driving hours."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Any thirty consecutive non-driving minutes satisfy that break, including "
"loading or inspection. They do not necessarily reset the duty window."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Both hours modes use these limits. Relaxed changes enforcement pressure. "
"One warning comes before each limit: one hour left in the Relaxed driving "
"mode, two hours in Standard, and two hours, one hour and thirty minutes in "
"Real time. None comes for a limit the trip ends inside."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "Check again as traffic or weather changes."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_hos_wheel}, {control_hos_break}, {control_hos_drive}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid ""
"{control_hos_wheel} reads time used, {control_hos_break} the break, and "
"{control_hos_drive} the shift limits and reachable rest."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_hos_wheel}, {control_hos_break}, {control_hos_drive}
msgid ""
"{control_hos_wheel} reads time used, {control_hos_break} the break, and "
"{control_hos_drive} the shift limits and reachable rest. Check again as "
"traffic or weather changes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Ten-hour sleep is the simplest reset. Supported sleeper parking offers two, "
"three, seven, or eight hours for an eight-plus-two or seven-plus-three "
"split."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The long split pauses the duty window. The short half counts until the pair "
"completes. A nap that leaves the window running tells you when it closes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fatigue rises faster at night and reduces reaction time. Respond to nod-off "
"warnings by steering or braking. Repeated misses can force you off the road."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Meals and coffee help temporarily. A half-hour meal counts as a break. "
"Proper sleep clears fatigue; a legal reset with poor rest can leave you "
"tired."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A stop offers only its listed services. A full parking lot can still sell "
"diesel. A motel may offer full rest at your expense."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sleep 10 hours in the lot is poor rest. Sleeper parking gives fully-rested "
"ten-hour sleep."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_rest}
msgid ""
"Away from route points and fully stopped, {control_rest} or the pause menu "
"offers emergency shoulder sleep: ten hours pass, with poor rest and "
"possible parking ticket or minor damage."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The deadline keeps running during all rest. Logbook at the terminal and the "
"ELD app let you review duty and limits."
msgstr ""

msgid "Career, equipment, and money"
msgstr "Sự nghiệp, thiết bị và tiền bạc"

msgid ""
"New company hires get an assigned load. Load choice opens at level eight. "
"Declining costs trust; low trust can remove load choice again."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Jobs name cargo, weight, pay, deadline, facilities, and equipment "
"requirements. F1 reads the details. Fuel adds weight; check before filling "
"a marginal load."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Walk around a dropped trailer before leaving. A defect can be refused at "
"the yard or found later at inspection."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Company drivers receive wages and bonuses. Owners receive higher gross with "
"fuel, repair, reserves, trailer charges, and fees to pay."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Settlement separates gross pay, carrier-paid or reimbursed charges, driver "
"costs, and net driver pay. On-time and undamaged freight pays better."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Unpaid charges become a balance owed. Later settlements use one quarter for "
"debt and advances together, leaving three quarters as take-home."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Debt warnings name the ceiling and consequence. At the ceiling, a company "
"driver changes carrier or an owner loses tractors and returns to company "
"driving."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You keep career level, experience, endorsements, and record. Career stats "
"reads debt and trust; Business status explains ownership requirements."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The garage refuels, repairs, replaces tires, and services brakes and "
"engines. Company routine costs use the carrier account; owners can buy "
"partial service when cash is short."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"At eighty percent component wear, arrange service. At one hundred, that "
"component puts the truck out of service. Damage has separate reduced-power, "
"limp-mode, and out-of-service bands."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Owners buy tractors, upgrades, and trailer programs. Each truck keeps its "
"condition; upgrades apply across the fleet."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Licenses and training opens refrigerated, heavy-haul, high-value, liquid "
"bulk, doubles, hazardous, port, and long-combination freight as "
"requirements clear."
msgstr ""

msgid "The garage and freight markets"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each metro represents a wider freight area with many shippers: rail and "
"intermodal ramps, parcel hubs, farms, grain elevators, chemical terminals, "
"and other facilities."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Facilities determine local cargo. Dispatch routes include stops for fuel "
"and legal rest; F1 reads the load's requirements before you accept it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Owners can add reefer, flatbed, and bulk programs. Company trailers cover "
"the equipment requirements of approved loads."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An engine tune adds pulling power. An aerodynamic kit reduces highway fuel "
"burn. A long-range tank adds fifty gallons; reinforced brakes resist fade "
"longer."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Company equipment improves with seniority. Low trust can hold it back until "
"your record and finances recover."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Terminal garages offer repair, tires, brakes, engine service, and washing. "
"Road stops offer only the services listed for that location."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Damage above fifty percent reduces power; above seventy-five brings limp "
"mode and a forty-five mile per hour cap. Above ninety puts the truck out of "
"service."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A roadside mechanic can help during a trip. Stop safely and use the pause "
"menu or Call dispatch for help."
msgstr ""

msgid "Winter equipment"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Winter tires improve snow and ice grip. Chains are carried until you "
"install them while stopped through the pause menu."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Chain laws require chains on a truck at every level. Winter tires don't "
"count for a semi. The exceptions are level one in Colorado and Oregon, "
"which chain only single-drive-axle trucks, and in Wyoming, which accepts "
"snow tires. Signs announce the requirement before the chain-up area."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Chain work uses on-duty time and adds fatigue, especially at night. Keep "
"under chain speed, 30 miles per hour or 48 kilometers per hour, and remove "
"chains on bare pavement before they break."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Worn tires and strong engine braking make slippery roads harder to control. "
"Stop for rest or safer conditions when necessary."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "Escape returns."
msgstr "Nhấn Escape để quay lại."

#. placeholders: {control_status}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "Open driving status with {control_status}, then choose Driver apps."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_status}
msgid ""
"Open driving status with {control_status}, then choose Driver apps. Up and "
"Down choose an app; Enter opens it. Escape returns."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "Up and Down choose an app; Enter opens it."
msgstr "Dùng Up và Down để chọn ứng dụng; nhấn Enter để mở."

msgid ""
"In a report, Up and Down move through the information and Enter repeats "
"what you selected. Escape returns to Driver apps, then to driving status."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Radio lets you switch the radio on or off, tune, manage favorites, and "
"suggest a station. Search by part of a name, call sign, or format, then "
"choose a result. Out-of-range stations cannot be tuned here."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Navigation reviews your next guidance, progress, and next listed exit. Map "
"under driving status gives a broader view of the route and stops."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Weather gives conditions, suggested safe speed, how old the report is, and "
"any active live weather alerts. Simulated weather includes a forecast; a "
"live report may not. The app tells you if a live check is updating or has "
"failed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Traffic reports traffic ahead, including a reported vehicle's distance and "
"speed. No reported pinch in the next twenty miles does not guarantee an "
"empty road."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Truck stops lists up to three route stops in the next hundred miles, with "
"distance and services. Check for fuel, repairs, and parking before choosing "
"a stop."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "Enforcement reports are quiet in hours modes without enforcement."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "Road chatter gives informal driver reports that may be stale."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_cb}
msgid ""
"Road chatter gives informal driver reports that may be stale. Enforcement "
"reports are quiet in hours modes without enforcement. {control_cb} repeats "
"the last chatter with its distance updated."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_cb}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "{control_cb} repeats the last chatter with its distance updated."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"ELD gives your hours and guidance about reachable legal rest. Check again "
"if traffic or weather slows your trip."
msgstr ""

msgid "Radio and playlists"
msgstr "Đài phát thanh và danh sách phát"

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid ""
"Page Down or apostrophe tunes forward; Page Up or semicolon tunes backward."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_radio}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid ""
"With the engine running, {control_radio} switches the radio on or off."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_radio}
msgid ""
"With the engine running, {control_radio} switches the radio on or off. Page "
"Down or apostrophe tunes forward; Page Up or semicolon tunes backward."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hold Control with a tune key to jump between categories, including route "
"music, Freight Fate stations, your playlists, favorites, and broadcast or "
"web stations."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hold Shift to change volume in ten percent steps: Page Up or semicolon "
"raises it, Page Down or apostrophe lowers it."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_radio_favorite}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "{control_radio_favorite} saves or removes a favorite."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_radio_favorite}, {control_radio_status}, {control_radio_now_playing}
msgid ""
"{control_radio_favorite} saves or removes a favorite. "
"{control_radio_status} reads station, reception, volume, and streamer-safe "
"status. {control_radio_now_playing} reads available song information."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_radio_now_playing}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "{control_radio_now_playing} reads available song information."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_radio_status}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid ""
"{control_radio_status} reads station, reception, volume, and streamer-safe "
"status."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Radio status lists receivable stations. Use the Radio app to choose or "
"search for a station and browse favorites."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Regional stations fade as you leave their range. Favorites play from "
"anywhere and never fade. If reception fails, the radio tries a clear local "
"station, then a fallback. Failed streams leave the dial for that session. "
"Roadhouse and Night Line are available across the map."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Put M3U, M3U8, or PLS playlists in the Playlists folder inside your saves "
"folder. Radio status tells you the folder location and reloads it when "
"opened. Entries can be audio files, network paths, or stream addresses."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Personal playlists normally play in order and resume where you left them. "
"Shuffle plays every track once in a random order, then chooses a new order. "
"Unreadable entries are skipped."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Original music uses licensed menu and Roadhouse tracks. Synthesized uses "
"music the game composes and the original three tracks, removing fictional "
"regional stations and voiced breaks. Real streams and personal playlists "
"remain unless streamer-safe mode hides them."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Streamer-safe mode keeps built-in safe stations. With Synthesized music, "
"only the synthesized Roadhouse remains. Radio power, volume, and now "
"playing still work; other station controls do nothing."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Suggest a station in the Radio app asks for its type, name, and stream "
"address. AM and FM suggestions also need a call sign and state. City and "
"frequency are optional. Connect an account and enable Online services first."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Suggestions are checked for playback and duplicates before review. Accepted "
"stations can appear at a later launch without a game update."
msgstr ""

msgid "Settings and accessibility"
msgstr "Cài đặt và trợ năng"

msgid ""
"Settings save as you change them. Choose a setting with Up or Down, then "
"Right or Enter for its next value, or Left for the previous value."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Gameplay holds driving assistance, difficulty and hours, world and traffic, "
"and controls. Audio, Speech, Updates, Problem reports, and Online have "
"separate choices where supported. F1 explains the selected setting."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Realistic leaves lane keeping off. Balanced adds partial lane keeping and "
"facility stops. All assists adds full lane keeping and a fifty-five mile "
"per hour descent ceiling. Adjusting assistance yourself changes the preset "
"name to Custom."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Presets leave driving pace, legal hours, transmission, world sources, "
"latching brake, and cue volumes as they are."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Relaxed pacing passes about ten minutes of road and clock each real minute, "
"with more response time and gentler consequences. Standard moves twice as "
"fast. Real time follows the computer clock at real speed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Change pacing mid-drive from pause; it begins when the truck next stops. "
"Legal hours and time remaining on a deadline stay intact."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose simulated or available live weather, traffic, and parking separately "
"from online sharing. Fuel prices can use the weekly national diesel average "
"with regional differences or simulated regional prices."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Adjust music, radio, engine, weather, and gameplay cues separately if one "
"covers another. Game sounds step back for speech lowers engine, weather, "
"and radio to half volume while the road voice speaks."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Driving speech chooses Standard, Quiet, or Urgent only announcements. "
"Readout keys still answer when asked. Place names and roadside chatter have "
"separate controls."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Speech and braille sends messages to both. Braille only requires NVDA or "
"JAWS; speech returns if the screen reader closes. You can also choose a "
"separate driving event voice."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For a problem report, use Where the game log is saved to find the session "
"record, including spoken messages. It stays on your computer unless you "
"share it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Online sharing and backups"
msgstr "Chia sẻ trực tuyến và sao lưu"

msgid ""
"Online lets you browse driver profiles and account achievements, connect an "
"account, choose sharing, and manage private backups. Viewing drivers shares "
"nothing about you."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Drivers on duty refreshes about once a minute. Enter opens a driver's "
"public profile. Driver directory includes drivers who are not currently "
"playing; Check again refreshes it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use an activation code in your browser to connect an existing account and "
"enable profile sharing and backup. You can turn either off afterward."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Profile sharing includes your activity, achievements, and road journal. "
"Public profiles omit current cash, full saves, coordinates, and precise "
"location. Career statistics need an accepted private backup."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Cloud backup keeps ten accepted revisions per career and up to ten careers. "
"Restore checks the signed backup and keeps the replaced local save as a "
"fallback. Back up this career now uploads immediately."
msgstr ""

msgid "Discord shows broad activity and clears it after half an hour idle."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Online services switches sharing services off together while remembering "
"your choices. Live weather, traffic, and parking keep their separate "
"settings."
msgstr ""

msgid "Common questions"
msgstr "Câu hỏi thường gặp"

msgid ""
"Do I have to buy a truck? No. The carrier assigns company drivers a truck "
"and pays its fuel, repairs, and insurance. Buying trucks opens with the "
"owner-operator buy-in from level 18; Business status lists what else it "
"needs."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"What are the fleets on Career stats? Each is a set of carrier trucks that "
"dispatch assigns by level: the yard standard, then the regional fleet at "
"level 4, the long-haul fleet at 9, the premium fleet at 13, and first pick "
"of the yard at 17. Moving up costs you nothing."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Why am I in a different truck on some loads? Until level 9, dispatch "
"matches a spare truck to each load. From level 9 you keep one truck for "
"every load until dispatch moves you up to the next fleet."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Why am I not in the truck my level earns? Low dispatch trust, a suspended "
"CDL, debt, or your driving record can hold equipment back. Career stats "
"names the reason and what brings the truck back."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"What is the difference between reputation and dispatch trust? Reputation is "
"a score from your deliveries, lowered by your driving record: Outstanding, "
"Well regarded, Established, Unproven, Shaky, Damaged, or Ruined. New "
"drivers start at 50, Unproven. A trust line shows it as, for example, "
"Dispatch trust: full. Reputation 85 out of 100. Dispatch trust is what the "
"carrier lets you do right now; your CDL, your record, and what you owe "
"count toward it too. Settings, Speech has Score display: both, percentage "
"only, or description only."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Why can I not accept a load? It may need a certificate, endorsement, or "
"trailer you do not have. F1 on the load reads its requirements, and "
"Licenses and training offers the courses."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "Open weigh station ahead means every truck must pull in."
msgstr "Có trạm cân bắt buộc phía trước; mọi xe tải đều phải vào trạm."

#. placeholders: {control_take_exit}, {control_rest}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid ""
"Signal with {control_take_exit}, stop at the scale, then press "
"{control_rest} to check in."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "Why did I get a citation at a weigh station?"
msgstr "Vì sao tôi bị phạt tại trạm cân?"

#. placeholders: {control_take_exit}, {control_rest}
msgid ""
"Why did I get a citation at a weigh station? Open weigh station ahead means "
"every truck must pull in. Signal with {control_take_exit}, stop at the "
"scale, then press {control_rest} to check in."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "Some states hold trucks below the car limit."
msgstr "Một số bang áp dụng giới hạn tốc độ cho xe tải thấp hơn xe con."

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "Why is the limit 55 on a fast highway?"
msgstr "Vì sao giới hạn tốc độ là 55 trên đường cao tốc?"

#. placeholders: {control_speed_limit}
msgid ""
"Why is the limit 55 on a fast highway? Some states hold trucks below the "
"car limit. {control_speed_limit} names the state when it does."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_speed_limit}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "{control_speed_limit} names the state when it does."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "I missed my exit."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_route}
msgid ""
"I missed my exit. What now? Keep driving and follow the turnaround "
"guidance. {control_route} reads the distance left."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "Keep driving and follow the turnaround guidance."
msgstr "Tiếp tục lái xe và làm theo hướng dẫn quay đầu."

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "What now?"
msgstr "Bây giờ làm gì?"

#. placeholders: {control_route}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "{control_route} reads the distance left."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The truck will not move. What should I check? Fuel, the engine, air "
"pressure, and the parking brake. Damage, worn parts, or a suspended CDL can "
"also stop you."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "How do I know when a hill ends?"
msgstr "Làm sao biết khi nào hết dốc?"

#. placeholders: {control_grade}
msgid ""
"How do I know when a hill ends? {control_grade} reads the grade under the "
"wheels and the next one worth planning for."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_grade}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid ""
"{control_grade} reads the grade under the wheels and the next one worth "
"planning for."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid "How do I change stations or play my own music?"
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_radio}
msgid ""
"How do I change stations or play my own music? With the engine running, "
"{control_radio} switches the radio on, and Page Up or Page Down tunes. Put "
"playlist files in the Playlists folder inside your saves folder; Radio "
"status says where it is."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid ""
"Put playlist files in the Playlists folder inside your saves folder; Radio "
"status says where it is."
msgstr ""

#. placeholders: {control_radio}
#. one sentence of a longer line
msgid ""
"With the engine running, {control_radio} switches the radio on, and Page Up "
"or Page Down tunes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Can I hear a weather warning again? With live weather on, the Weather app "
"under Driver apps lists active alerts. Comma also steps back through recent "
"messages."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Can I steer myself? Yes. Choose the Realistic preset, or set lane keeping "
"to off, under Settings, Gameplay, Driving assistance."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Can I play in braille only? Set Output to braille only under Settings, "
"Speech. It needs NVDA or JAWS."
msgstr ""

msgid "Controller"
msgstr "Tay cầm điều khiển"

msgid ""
"Controllers work alongside the keyboard. Button names use the Xbox layout. "
"Settings, Gameplay, Controls lets you change eligible assignments."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On newer Xbox controllers, Back is the View button, left of the Xbox "
"button, and Start is the Menu button on its right. On Windows, the Xbox "
"button opens the Game Bar; press it again to return."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In menus, D-pad moves, A confirms, B returns, and Back reads help. During "
"driving speech, Back stops the voice; otherwise it reads help. Start pauses."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Right trigger accelerates, left trigger brakes, and fully pressing the left "
"trigger gives emergency braking. The left stick steers; with lane keeping "
"on full, push it left or right to change one lane."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To reverse in automatic, stop, release the left trigger, then press and "
"hold it again. Use a fresh right-trigger hold at a standstill for forward."
msgstr ""

#. one sentence of a longer line
